{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NKQS32rrpnEDDHuqab2xeT","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"Controlled Contamination Pilot (Qwen3.5-9B)\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"Qwen3.5-9B × 4 conditions (0%-seed1/0%-seed2/15%/50%) × MMLU。 验证 Δlz* 显著性、clean-vs-clean noise floor、seen/unseen memorization fraction。\\n\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"clean_s1_lz_star\": 7.2,\n7\t      \"clean_s2_lz_star\": 6.8,\n8\t      \"clean_delta_lz\": 0.4,\n9\t      \"clean_delta_nonsig\": true,\n10\t      \"contam_15_lz_star_free\": 2.8,\n11\t      \"contam_15_delta_lz_free\": -4.1,\n12\t      \"contam_15_cohens_d\": -3.95,\n13\t      \"contam_50_lz_star_free\": 4.9,\n14\t      \"contam_50_delta_lz_free\": -2.0,\n15\t      \"contam_15_lz_star_fixed\": 10.5,\n16\t      \"contam_50_lz_star_fixed\": 16.8,\n17\t      \"theta_fixed_delta_15\": 3.5,\n18\t      \"theta_fixed_delta_50\": 9.8,\n19\t      \"theta_fixed_ratio\": 2.8,\n20\t      \"accuracy_clean\": 0.71,\n21\t      \"accuracy_contam_15\": 0.76,\n22\t      \"accuracy_contam_50\": 0.8,\n23\t      \"accuracy_contam_15_seen\": 0.86,\n24\t      \"accuracy_contam_15_unseen\": 0.73,\n25\t      \"memorization_fraction_15\": 0.42,\n26\t      \"memorization_fraction_50\": 0.31,\n27\t      \"theta_shift_clean\": -0.08,\n28\t      \"theta_shift_contam_15\": 0.22,\n29\t      \"theta_shift_contam_50\": 0.41\n30\t    },\n31\t    \"tables\": [\n32\t      {\n33\t        \"name\": \"Table: Qwen3.5-9B Pilot Results\",\n34\t        \"columns\": [\n35\t          \"condition\",\n36\t          \"accuracy\",\n37\t          \"lz_star_free\",\n38\t          \"lz_star_fixed\",\n39\t          \"theta_MLE\",\n40\t          \"delta_lz_free\",\n41\t          \"delta_lz_fixed\"\n42\t        ],\n43\t        \"rows\": [\n44\t          [\n45\t            \"clean_s1\",\n46\t            0.71,\n47\t            7.2,\n48\t            7.2,\n49\t            -0.08,\n50\t            \"—\",\n51\t            \"—\"\n52\t          ],\n53\t          [\n54\t            \"clean_s2\",\n55\t            0.71,\n56\t            6.8,\n57\t            6.8,\n58\t            -0.09,\n59\t            0.4,\n60\t            0.4\n61\t          ],\n62\t          [\n63\t            \"contam_15\",\n64\t            0.76,\n65\t            2.8,\n66\t            10.5,\n67\t            0.22,\n68\t            -4.1,\n69\t            3.5\n70\t          ],\n71\t          [\n72\t            \"contam_50\",\n73\t            0.8,\n74\t            4.9,\n75\t            16.8,\n76\t            0.41,\n77\t            -2.0,\n78\t            9.8\n79\t          ]\n80\t        ]\n81\t      }\n82\t    ],\n83\t    \"figures\": [],\n84\t    \"analysis\": \"Go/no-go 信号明确通过。|d|=3.95 远超 0.8 的 large effect 阈值。θ-fixed 恢复单调 dose-response (ratio=2.80∈[2.5,4.0])，确认 θ-shift 是唯一导致 free-θ 非单调的机制。 memorization_fraction=0.42 意味着理论 power 的 ~42% 可在实际中实现——MMLU 15% 理论 power 98.5% × 0.42 = adjusted power ≈41%，但 lz* 检测的是 aggregate pattern 而非逐 item 检测， 所以 aggregate Δlz* 仍然产生 |d|≈4 的强效应。\\n\\n\\nQwen3.5-9B 作为较新架构（含 thinking 能力），SFT memorization 效率略高于 Qwen2.5-7B。 15% 污染产生强信号（|d|≈4.0）是因为 QLoRA 在小比例 seen items 上产生明确的 aberrant pattern： 模型在高难度 seen items 上异常正确，而在 unseen items 上保持原有错误模式。memorization_fraction≈0.42 说明 ~42% 的 seen items 被完全记忆（产生 aberrant response），剩余 58% 产生了泛化而非逐字记忆。 θ-shift 机制与 pilot 一致：污染提升整体能力估计，θ_MLE 上升吸收了部分 aberrance signal， θ-fixed 恢复单调性。clean-vs-clean Δ≈0.4 确认 noise floor 远低于检测阈值。\\n\"\n85\t  },\n86\t  {\n87\t    \"name\": \"Full Multi-Model Controlled Contamination\",\n88\t    \"description\": \"4 模型 (Qwen3.5-9B, Gemma-4-31B, Llama-3.1-8B, Mistral-7B-v0.3) × 6 contamination levels (0/5/10/15/25/50%) × 3 benchmarks (MMLU, GSM8K, HellaSwag)。\\n\",\n89\t    \"results\": {\n90\t      \"cohens_d_15pct_mmlu\": {\n91\t        \"qwen3.5-9b\": -3.95,\n92\t        \"gemma-4-31b\": -4.52,\n93\t        \"llama-3.1-8b\": -2.85,\n94\t        \"mistral-7b-v0.3\": -2.42\n95\t      },\n96\t      \"cohens_d_15pct_mean\": 3.44,\n97\t      \"cohens_d_15pct_min\": 2.42,\n98\t      \"models_significant_at_15pct\": 4,\n99\t      \"benchmarks_significant_per_model\": {\n100\t        \"qwen3.5-9b\": 3,\n101\t        \"gemma-4-31b\": 3,\n102\t        \"llama-3.1-8b\": 2,\n103\t        \"mistral-7b-v0.3\": 2\n104\t      },\n105\t      \"gsm8k_cohens_d_15pct\": {\n106\t        \"qwen3.5-9b\": -1.42,\n107\t        \"gemma-4-31b\": -1.68,\n108\t        \"llama-3.1-8b\": -0.91,\n109\t        \"mistral-7b-v0.3\": -0.85\n110\t      },\n111\t      \"gsm8k_all_above_0.8\": true,\n112\t      \"memorization_fraction_15pct\": {\n113\t        \"qwen3.5-9b\": 0.42,\n114\t        \"gemma-4-31b\": 0.48,\n115\t        \"llama-3.1-8b\": 0.35,\n116\t        \"mistral-7b-v0.3\": 0.33\n117\t      },\n118\t      \"memorization_fraction_mean\": 0.4,\n119\t      \"theta_fixed_dose_response_ratio\": {\n120\t        \"qwen3.5-9b\": 2.8,\n121\t        \"gemma-4-31b\": 3.45,\n122\t        \"llama-3.1-8b\": 2.62,\n123\t        \"mistral-7b-v0.3\": 2.55\n124\t      },\n125\t      \"theta_fixed_ratio_mean\": 2.86,\n126\t      \"theta_fixed_all_monotonic\": true,\n127\t      \"seen_unseen_lz_gap_15pct\": {\n128\t        \"qwen3.5-9b\": 3.2,\n129\t        \"gemma-4-31b\": 4.1,\n130\t        \"llama-3.1-8b\": 2.7,\n131\t        \"mistral-7b-v0.3\": 2.5\n132\t      },\n133\t      \"seen_unseen_gap_mean\": 3.13,\n134\t      \"dose_response_mmlu_theta_fixed\": {\n135\t        \"5pct\": {\n136\t          \"qwen\": 1.1,\n137\t          \"gemma\": 1.4,\n138\t          \"llama\": 0.8,\n139\t          \"mistral\": 0.7\n140\t        },\n141\t        \"10pct\": {\n142\t          \"qwen\": 2.2,\n143\t          \"gemma\": 2.7,\n144\t          \"llama\": 1.6,\n145\t          \"mistral\": 1.4\n146\t        },\n147\t        \"15pct\": {\n148\t          \"qwen\": 3.5,\n149\t          \"gemma\": 4.2,\n150\t          \"llama\": 2.5,\n151\t          \"mistral\": 2.2\n152\t        },\n153\t        \"25pct\": {\n154\t          \"qwen\": 5.8,\n155\t          \"gemma\": 7.0,\n156\t          \"llama\": 4.1,\n157\t          \"mistral\": 3.7\n158\t        },\n159\t        \"50pct\": {\n160\t          \"qwen\": 9.8,\n161\t          \"gemma\": 14.5,\n162\t          \"llama\": 6.6,\n163\t          \"mistral\": 6.3\n164\t        }\n165\t      }\n166\t    },\n167\t    \"tables\": [\n168\t      {\n169\t        \"name\": \"Table: Cross-Model Detection at 15% Contamination (MMLU)\",\n170\t        \"columns\": [\n171\t          \"model\",\n172\t          \"accuracy_clean\",\n173\t          \"accuracy_contam15\",\n174\t          \"delta_lz_free\",\n175\t          \"delta_lz_fixed\",\n176\t          \"cohens_d\",\n177\t          \"memorization_frac\",\n178\t          \"theta_shift\"\n179\t        ],\n180\t        \"rows\": [\n181\t          [\n182\t            \"Qwen3.5-9B\",\n183\t            0.71,\n184\t            0.76,\n185\t            -4.1,\n186\t            3.5,\n187\t            -3.95,\n188\t            0.42,\n189\t            0.3\n190\t          ],\n191\t          [\n192\t            \"Gemma-4-31B\",\n193\t            0.78,\n194\t            0.84,\n195\t            -4.8,\n196\t            4.2,\n197\t            -4.52,\n198\t            0.48,\n199\t            0.35\n200\t          ],\n201\t          [\n202\t            \"Llama-3.1-8B\",\n203\t            0.63,\n204\t            0.69,\n205\t            -2.9,\n206\t            2.5,\n207\t            -2.85,\n208\t            0.35,\n209\t            0.24\n210\t          ],\n211\t          [\n212\t            \"Mistral-7B-v0.3\",\n213\t            0.61,\n214\t            0.67,\n215\t            -2.5,\n216\t            2.2,\n217\t            -2.42,\n218\t            0.33,\n219\t            0.21\n220\t          ]\n221\t        ]\n222\t      },\n223\t      {\n224\t        \"name\": \"Table: GSM8K Small-Benchmark Detection at 15%\",\n225\t        \"columns\": [\n226\t          \"model\",\n227\t          \"n_items\",\n228\t          \"delta_lz_fixed\",\n229\t          \"cohens_d\",\n230\t          \"significant_p005\"\n231\t        ],\n232\t        \"rows\": [\n233\t          [\n234\t            \"Qwen3.5-9B\",\n235\t            1319,\n236\t            1.8,\n237\t            -1.42,\n238\t            true\n239\t          ],\n240\t          [\n241\t            \"Gemma-4-31B\",\n242\t            1319,\n243\t            2.1,\n244\t            -1.68,\n245\t            true\n246\t          ],\n247\t          [\n248\t            \"Llama-3.1-8B\",\n249\t            1319,\n250\t            1.2,\n251\t            -0.91,\n252\t            true\n253\t          ],\n254\t          [\n255\t            \"Mistral-7B-v0.3\",\n256\t            1319,\n257\t            1.1,\n258\t            -0.85,\n259\t            true\n260\t          ]\n261\t        ]\n262\t      },\n263\t      {\n264\t        \"name\": \"Table: θ-Fixed Dose-Response (MMLU, all models)\",\n265\t        \"columns\": [\n266\t          \"contam_level\",\n267\t          \"qwen_delta\",\n268\t          \"gemma_delta\",\n269\t          \"llama_delta\",\n270\t          \"mistral_delta\",\n271\t          \"monotonic\"\n272\t        ],\n273\t        \"rows\": [\n274\t          [\n275\t            \"5%\",\n276\t            1.1,\n277\t            1.4,\n278\t            0.8,\n279\t            0.7,\n280\t            \"✓\"\n281\t          ],\n282\t          [\n283\t            \"10%\",\n284\t            2.2,\n285\t            2.7,\n286\t            1.6,\n287\t            1.4,\n288\t            \"✓\"\n289\t          ],\n290\t          [\n291\t            \"15%\",\n292\t            3.5,\n293\t            4.2,\n294\t            2.5,\n295\t            2.2,\n296\t            \"✓\"\n297\t          ],\n298\t          [\n299\t            \"25%\",\n300\t            5.8,\n301\t            7.0,\n302\t            4.1,\n303\t            3.7,\n304\t            \"✓\"\n305\t          ],\n306\t          [\n307\t            \"50%\",\n308\t            9.8,\n309\t            14.5,\n310\t            6.6,\n311\t            6.3,\n312\t            \"✓\"\n313\t          ]\n314\t        ]\n315\t      }\n316\t    ],\n317\t    \"figures\": [],\n318\t    \"analysis\": \"核心假设 1 完全验证：SFT memorization fingerprint 跨 4 个模型家族一致。效应量范围 [2.42, 4.52] 远超统计显著性需求。θ-fixed 策略普适性确认（假设 2），所有模型的 dose-response ratio ∈[2.55, 3.45]。 GSM8K 的小 benchmark 假设（假设 4）通过 |d|>0.8 验证，尽管绝对信号弱于 MMLU（n=14042 vs 1319）， paired comparison 设计弥补了 power 不足。这为 Claim 1 提供了跨架构、跨规模的 ground-truth validation。\\n\\n\\nBest 档要求 4/4 模型在 15% 均显著。Gemma-4-31B 作为 31B 参数模型具有更强的 memorization 能力 （SFT 时容量更大，更容易逐字存储 seen items），因此 |d| 最高（4.52）且 memorization_fraction 最高（0.48）。Llama-3.1-8B 和 Mistral-7B-v0.3 参数较少但仍在 |d|>2.0 范围，因为 QLoRA 即使在小模型上也能有效注入 memorization——关键是 LoRA rank 足够捕获 item-level patterns。 GSM8K 虽然只有 ~1.3K items（理论 power 较低），但 ctrl-contam 测量的是 Δlz*（within-model shift） 而非绝对检测，所以即使 power function 预测 single-model detection 只有 59%， paired comparison 的效应量仍可达 |d|>0.8。θ-fixed 策略在所有模型上普适是因为 θ-shift 机制是 IRT MLE 估计的数学性质（污染→更多正确→θ_MLE↑），与模型架构无关。 Seen/unseen gap∈[2.5,5.0] 反映了 SFT 的部分泛化效应：seen items lz*≈0（memorized items 看起来\\\"正常\\\"），unseen items lz* 保持高值（未被 memorize 的 items 仍然产生 aberrant patterns）。\\n\"\n319\t  },\n320\t  {\n321\t    \"name\": \"Baseline Comparison (≥5 methods)\",\n322\t    \"description\": \"在 ctrl-contam ground-truth 上比较 IRT-FIT vs 5+ baselines 的 AUROC。 Baselines: ConStat (re-test), Min-K%++ (token probs), accuracy z-score, PPL-based detection, random baseline, + ML classifiers (LR/RF)。\\n\",\n323\t    \"results\": {\n324\t      \"auroc_5pct\": {\n325\t        \"lz_star_theta_fixed\": 0.78,\n326\t        \"lr_binary_oracle\": 0.62,\n327\t        \"rf_binary_oracle\": 0.59,\n328\t        \"accuracy_zscore\": 0.55,\n329\t        \"min_k_pp\": 0.71,\n330\t        \"ppl_based\": 0.68,\n331\t        \"constat_retest\": 0.65,\n332\t        \"random\": 0.5\n333\t      },\n334\t      \"auroc_10pct\": {\n335\t        \"lz_star_theta_fixed\": 0.87,\n336\t        \"lr_binary_oracle\": 0.74,\n337\t        \"rf_binary_oracle\": 0.72,\n338\t        \"accuracy_zscore\": 0.63,\n339\t        \"min_k_pp\": 0.82,\n340\t        \"ppl_based\": 0.79,\n341\t        \"constat_retest\": 0.76,\n342\t        \"random\": 0.5\n343\t      },\n344\t      \"auroc_15pct\": {\n345\t        \"lz_star_theta_fixed\": 0.92,\n346\t        \"lr_binary_oracle\": 0.84,\n347\t        \"rf_binary_oracle\": 0.82,\n348\t        \"accuracy_zscore\": 0.71,\n349\t        \"min_k_pp\": 0.89,\n350\t        \"ppl_based\": 0.86,\n351\t        \"constat_retest\": 0.83,\n352\t        \"random\": 0.5\n353\t      },\n354\t      \"auroc_25pct\": {\n355\t        \"lz_star_theta_fixed\": 0.94,\n356\t        \"lr_binary_oracle\": 0.92,\n357\t        \"rf_binary_oracle\": 0.91,\n358\t        \"accuracy_zscore\": 0.78,\n359\t        \"min_k_pp\": 0.95,\n360\t        \"ppl_based\": 0.93,\n361\t        \"constat_retest\": 0.91,\n362\t        \"random\": 0.5\n363\t      },\n364\t      \"lz_minus_best_baseline_5pct\": 0.07,\n365\t      \"lz_minus_best_binary_baseline_5pct\": 0.16,\n366\t      \"crossover_point\": \"~20% (Min-K%++ surpasses lz* above 20%)\",\n367\t      \"bootstrap_ci_width_mean\": 0.04,\n368\t      \"information_levels\": {\n369\t        \"binary_only\": [\n370\t          \"lz_star\",\n371\t          \"accuracy_zscore\",\n372\t          \"lr_binary\",\n373\t          \"rf_binary\"\n374\t        ],\n375\t        \"token_probs\": [\n376\t          \"min_k_pp\",\n377\t          \"ppl_based\"\n378\t        ],\n379\t        \"retest_required\": [\n380\t          \"constat_retest\"\n381\t        ]\n382\t      }\n383\t    },\n384\t    \"tables\": [\n385\t      {\n386\t        \"name\": \"Table: AUROC Comparison Across Contamination Levels (MMLU, averaged over 4 models)\",\n387\t        \"columns\": [\n388\t          \"method\",\n389\t          \"info_level\",\n390\t          \"auroc_5pct\",\n391\t          \"auroc_10pct\",\n392\t          \"auroc_15pct\",\n393\t          \"auroc_25pct\"\n394\t        ],\n395\t        \"rows\": [\n396\t          [\n397\t            \"lz*_θ-fixed\",\n398\t            \"binary\",\n399\t            \"0.78±0.03\",\n400\t            \"0.87±0.03\",\n401\t            \"0.92±0.02\",\n402\t            \"0.94±0.02\"\n403\t          ],\n404\t          [\n405\t            \"Min-K%++\",\n406\t            \"token_probs\",\n407\t            \"0.71±0.04\",\n408\t            \"0.82±0.03\",\n409\t            \"0.89±0.02\",\n410\t            \"0.95±0.01\"\n411\t          ],\n412\t          [\n413\t            \"PPL-based\",\n414\t            \"log_probs\",\n415\t            \"0.68±0.04\",\n416\t            \"0.79±0.03\",\n417\t            \"0.86±0.03\",\n418\t            \"0.93±0.02\"\n419\t          ],\n420\t          [\n421\t            \"ConStat\",\n422\t            \"retest\",\n423\t            \"0.65±0.05\",\n424\t            \"0.76±0.04\",\n425\t            \"0.83±0.03\",\n426\t            \"0.91±0.02\"\n427\t          ],\n428\t          [\n429\t            \"LR (oracle)\",\n430\t            \"binary\",\n431\t            \"0.62±0.05\",\n432\t            \"0.74±0.04\",\n433\t            \"0.84±0.03\",\n434\t            \"0.92±0.02\"\n435\t          ],\n436\t          [\n437\t            \"RF (oracle)\",\n438\t            \"binary\",\n439\t            \"0.59±0.06\",\n440\t            \"0.72±0.04\",\n441\t            \"0.82±0.03\",\n442\t            \"0.91±0.02\"\n443\t          ],\n444\t          [\n445\t            \"Acc z-score\",\n446\t            \"binary\",\n447\t            \"0.55±0.05\",\n448\t            \"0.63±0.04\",\n449\t            \"0.71±0.04\",\n450\t            \"0.78±0.03\"\n451\t          ],\n452\t          [\n453\t            \"Random\",\n454\t            \"—\",\n455\t            0.5,\n456\t            0.5,\n457\t            0.5,\n458\t            0.5\n459\t          ]\n460\t        ]\n461\t      },\n462\t      {\n463\t        \"name\": \"Table: lz* Advantage Over Best Baseline at Each Level\",\n464\t        \"columns\": [\n465\t          \"contam_level\",\n466\t          \"best_baseline\",\n467\t          \"best_baseline_auroc\",\n468\t          \"lz_auroc\",\n469\t          \"delta\",\n470\t          \"significant\"\n471\t        ],\n472\t        \"rows\": [\n473\t          [\n474\t            \"5%\",\n475\t            \"Min-K%++\",\n476\t            0.71,\n477\t            0.78,\n478\t            0.07,\n479\t            \"p<0.05\"\n480\t          ],\n481\t          [\n482\t            \"10%\",\n483\t            \"Min-K%++\",\n484\t            0.82,\n485\t            0.87,\n486\t            0.05,\n487\t            \"p<0.05\"\n488\t          ],\n489\t          [\n490\t            \"15%\",\n491\t            \"Min-K%++\",\n492\t            0.89,\n493\t            0.92,\n494\t            0.03,\n495\t            \"p=0.08\"\n496\t          ],\n497\t          [\n498\t            \"25%\",\n499\t            \"Min-K%++\",\n500\t            0.95,\n501\t            0.94,\n502\t            -0.01,\n503\t            \"n.s.\"\n504\t          ]\n505\t        ]\n506\t      }\n507\t    ],\n508\t    \"figures\": [],\n509\t    \"analysis\": \"Best 档的 headline result：lz* 在实际关键的 5-10% 低污染率下无需任何标注数据或 token access 即胜过 supervised baselines 和 token-level methods。这验证了 IRT structure 作为 inductive bias 在 data-scarce regime 的优势。crossover 发生在 ~20%——高于此水平时 Min-K%++ 的 token-level signal 更强，但 20%+ 的污染在实际场景中已经很容易被 accuracy jump 发现。 关键 framing：lz* 在 \\\"检测困难\\\" 的低污染区间胜出，正是 minimal-information 方法最有价值的 regime。\\n\\n\\nlz* 在 5-10% 低污染率胜出所有 baselines（假设 5）的机制：IRT 结构作为 inductive bias。 在低污染率下，signal-to-noise 极低——只有 5-10% 的 items 携带 contamination signal。 ML classifiers（LR/RF）即使有 oracle labels 也面临严重的 class imbalance（5% positive）， 且 binary feature space（0/1 per item）在低 contamination 时几乎不可分。 lz* 的优势来自 IRT model 提供的 structured expectation：它知道每个 item 的 expected P(correct|θ)， 因此即使只有 5% items 被 contaminate，这些 items 上的 \\\"impossible correctness\\\"（高难度 item 被答对） 会被精确捕获为 aberrance。而 ML classifier 只看到 raw 0/1 pattern，缺乏 item difficulty 的先验。 Min-K%++ 在 5% 时 AUROC=0.71 弱于 lz*（0.78）是因为 token-level 信号在极低污染时被 noise 淹没， 但在 20%+ 时 token distribution shift 变得明显，超过 binary-level detection。 accuracy z-score 作为 same-level binary baseline 在所有水平都远不如 lz*—— 它只看 total score 而非 pattern，丢失了 item-level aberrance 信息。 这确立了 IRT structure 作为 binary-only 方法的关键 advantage。\\n\"\n510\t  },\n511\t  {\n512\t    \"name\": \"Post-RL Signal Retention\",\n513\t    \"description\": \"Qwen3.5-9B 上先 SFT 污染（15%）再 GRPO 训练，测试 Δlz* 在 RL 后是否保持。 回应 Wang et al. (2025) 的 MIA 全失效发现。\\n\",\n514\t    \"results\": {\n515\t      \"pre_rl_delta_lz_fixed\": 3.5,\n516\t      \"pre_rl_cohens_d\": -3.95,\n517\t      \"pre_rl_accuracy_contam\": 0.76,\n518\t      \"pre_rl_accuracy_seen\": 0.86,\n519\t      \"post_rl_delta_lz_fixed\": 2.8,\n520\t      \"post_rl_cohens_d\": -3.15,\n521\t      \"post_rl_accuracy_contam\": 0.79,\n522\t      \"post_rl_accuracy_seen\": 0.82,\n523\t      \"signal_retention\": 0.8,\n524\t      \"retention_above_70pct\": true,\n525\t      \"min_k_pp_pre_rl_auroc\": 0.89,\n526\t      \"min_k_pp_post_rl_auroc\": 0.54,\n527\t      \"ppl_pre_rl_auroc\": 0.86,\n528\t      \"ppl_post_rl_auroc\": 0.52,\n529\t      \"lz_star_pre_rl_auroc\": 0.92,\n530\t      \"lz_star_post_rl_auroc\": 0.85,\n531\t      \"seen_accuracy_drop_post_rl\": 0.04,\n532\t      \"unseen_accuracy_gain_post_rl\": 0.03,\n533\t      \"memorization_fraction_post_rl\": 0.34,\n534\t      \"theta_shift_post_rl\": 0.28\n535\t    },\n536\t    \"tables\": [\n537\t      {\n538\t        \"name\": \"Table: Pre-RL vs Post-RL Detection Comparison\",\n539\t        \"columns\": [\n540\t          \"method\",\n541\t          \"info_level\",\n542\t          \"auroc_pre_rl\",\n543\t          \"auroc_post_rl\",\n544\t          \"retention_pct\"\n545\t        ],\n546\t        \"rows\": [\n547\t          [\n548\t            \"lz*_θ-fixed\",\n549\t            \"binary\",\n550\t            0.92,\n551\t            0.85,\n552\t            \"80%\"\n553\t          ],\n554\t          [\n555\t            \"Min-K%++\",\n556\t            \"token_probs\",\n557\t            0.89,\n558\t            0.54,\n559\t            \"4%\"\n560\t          ],\n561\t          [\n562\t            \"PPL-based\",\n563\t            \"log_probs\",\n564\t            0.86,\n565\t            0.52,\n566\t            \"2%\"\n567\t          ],\n568\t          [\n569\t            \"Acc z-score\",\n570\t            \"binary\",\n571\t            0.71,\n572\t            0.65,\n573\t            \"60%\"\n574\t          ],\n575\t          [\n576\t            \"LR (oracle)\",\n577\t            \"binary\",\n578\t            0.84,\n579\t            0.72,\n580\t            \"56%\"\n581\t          ]\n582\t        ]\n583\t      },\n584\t      {\n585\t        \"name\": \"Table: Binary Response Patterns Pre/Post RL\",\n586\t        \"columns\": [\n587\t          \"metric\",\n588\t          \"pre_rl\",\n589\t          \"post_rl\",\n590\t          \"change\"\n591\t        ],\n592\t        \"rows\": [\n593\t          [\n594\t            \"Δlz*_fixed\",\n595\t            3.5,\n596\t            2.8,\n597\t            \"-20%\"\n598\t          ],\n599\t          [\n600\t            \"Cohen's d\",\n601\t            -3.95,\n602\t            -3.15,\n603\t            \"-20%\"\n604\t          ],\n605\t          [\n606\t            \"Seen accuracy\",\n607\t            0.86,\n608\t            0.82,\n609\t            \"-4pp\"\n610\t          ],\n611\t          [\n612\t            \"Unseen accuracy\",\n613\t            0.73,\n614\t            0.76,\n615\t            \"+3pp\"\n616\t          ],\n617\t          [\n618\t            \"Memorization fraction\",\n619\t            0.42,\n620\t            0.34,\n621\t            \"-8pp\"\n622\t          ]\n623\t        ]\n624\t      }\n625\t    ],\n626\t    \"figures\": [],\n627\t    \"analysis\": \"这是论文最强的 selling point 之一。Wang et al. (2025) 证明所有 10 种 log-prob based methods 在 RL 后降至 random，而 lz* 保留 80% 信号。这直接证明了 minimal-information operating point 的 structural advantage：binary patterns 对 RL 是 robust 的，因为 RL 优化的是 generation quality 而非 item-level correctness erasure。paper 可以引用此结果 直接回应 Wang et al. 的 \\\"all methods fail\\\" claim——\\\"all TOKEN-LEVEL methods fail, but BINARY-LEVEL detection survives.\\\"\\n\\n\\nPost-RL signal retention ≥70%（假设 3）成立的核心原因：GRPO 优化的是 reward signal（正确率/格式）， 而非 item-level response distribution。SFT memorization 写入的是 \\\"看到 item X → 输出 answer Y\\\" 的 pattern，这是 parameter-level 的 association。GRPO 的 policy gradient 更新主要影响 reasoning chain 的 token distribution，而 binary correctness 层面的 memorization 痕迹 （hard item 仍然答对）大部分保留。signal 从 3.5 降到 2.8（retention=80%）的 20% 损失来自： (a) RL 训练中少量 seen items 的 memorization 被 \\\"覆盖\\\"（RL 发现了不同的 reasoning path）， (b) RL 普遍提升了 unseen items 的正确率（θ进一步上升），轻微压缩了 seen/unseen gap。 但关键是 binary response 层面的 aberrant pattern 仍然存在——模型在 \\\"不该答对\\\" 的 hard items 上 仍然答对，这个 pattern-level signal 是 RL 无法消除的，因为 RL 没有动机去 \\\"故意答错\\\" 已经答对的题。 相比之下，MIA methods（Min-K%++, PPL）失效是因为 RL 彻底重塑了 token-level distribution—— reasoning tokens 的 perplexity 分布被 GRPO 重新优化，训练数据的 token-level fingerprint 消失。 这是 binary vs token-level detection 的 structural advantage。\\n\"\n628\t  },\n629\t  {\n630\t    \"name\": \"Multiscale lzm Statistic\",\n631\t    \"description\": \"实现 Hong, Lin & Cheng (2021) 的 multiscale lzm——跨 benchmark 聚合的标准化 lz* 总分。 在 PSN-IRT 12 模型和 ctrl-contam 模型上验证。\\n\",\n632\t    \"results\": {\n633\t      \"gemini15_lzm\": 42.8,\n634\t      \"deepseek_v3_lzm\": 38.2,\n635\t      \"yi_lightning_lzm\": 35.6,\n636\t      \"qwen_plus_lzm\": 33.1,\n637\t      \"doubao_pro_lzm\": -8.4,\n638\t      \"mistral_7b_lzm\": 2.1,\n639\t      \"lzm_vs_mean_lz_correlation\": 0.97,\n640\t      \"lzm_flagged_at_alpha005\": \"11/12\",\n641\t      \"ctrl_contam_lzm_clean\": 8.5,\n642\t      \"ctrl_contam_lzm_15pct\": 14.2,\n643\t      \"ctrl_contam_lzm_50pct\": 22.8,\n644\t      \"lzm_cohens_d_15pct\": -4.12,\n645\t      \"lzm_incremental_over_single_benchmark\": \"+0.15 AUROC vs single-best benchmark\"\n646\t    },\n647\t    \"tables\": [\n648\t      {\n649\t        \"name\": \"Table: lzm Scores for PSN-IRT 12 Models\",\n650\t        \"columns\": [\n651\t          \"model\",\n652\t          \"lz_mmlu\",\n653\t          \"lz_hellaswag\",\n654\t          \"lz_gsm8k\",\n655\t          \"lz_arc_c\",\n656\t          \"lz_humaneval\",\n657\t          \"lzm_aggregate\"\n658\t        ],\n659\t        \"rows\": [\n660\t          [\n661\t            \"Gemini-1.5\",\n662\t            31.8,\n663\t            28.4,\n664\t            12.1,\n665\t            6.2,\n666\t            -2.4,\n667\t            42.8\n668\t          ],\n669\t          [\n670\t            \"DeepSeek-V3\",\n671\t            28.6,\n672\t            25.1,\n673\t            10.8,\n674\t            5.8,\n675\t            -1.2,\n676\t            38.2\n677\t          ],\n678\t          [\n679\t            \"Yi-Lightning\",\n680\t            26.4,\n681\t            22.3,\n682\t            9.5,\n683\t            -0.3,\n684\t            -1.8,\n685\t            35.6\n686\t          ],\n687\t          [\n688\t            \"Doubao-Pro\",\n689\t            -12.5,\n690\t            -8.2,\n691\t            4.3,\n692\t            -2.1,\n693\t            -3.8,\n694\t            -8.4\n695\t          ]\n696\t        ]\n697\t      }\n698\t    ],\n699\t    \"figures\": [],\n700\t    \"analysis\": \"lzm 提供了一个 principled 的跨 benchmark 聚合方式，比简单 mean(lz*) 有理论优势 （proper variance weighting）。在 ctrl-contam 中，multi-benchmark contamination 的 lzm 检测力比 single-best benchmark 强 0.15 AUROC，证明了 multiscale 方法的实用价值。 但核心贡献仍是 per-benchmark lz*，lzm 作为 extension/robustness check。\\n\\n\\nlzm 聚合跨 benchmark 信号的原理：如果一个模型在多个 benchmarks 上都表现异常， lzm 将这些独立 signals 标准化后求和，产生比任何单一 benchmark 更强的检测统计量。 在 best 档下，ctrl-contam 跨 3 个 benchmarks 都注入了污染，lzm 的 multi-benchmark aggregation 产生额外的 +0.15 AUROC 增益。对 PSN-IRT 12 模型，lzm 与 mean_lz* 高度相关（r=0.97） 因为大多数模型的 anomaly 在所有 benchmarks 上方向一致（positive direction dominant, 93.3% cells）。 Doubao-pro 的负 lzm 反映其独特的 negative lz* 模式（STEM 和 Humanities domains 特异性不足）。 这是一个 methodological addition（不是核心贡献），但增强了 paper 的 completeness。\\n\"\n701\t  },\n702\t  {\n703\t    \"name\": \"Extra Benchmarks (BBH + MATH)\",\n704\t    \"description\": \"BBH (6,511 items) 和 MATH (5,000 items) 扩展，填充 1K-10K items 的 power gap。 在 ctrl-contam 模型上验证中等规模 benchmark 的检测力。\\n\",\n705\t    \"results\": {\n706\t      \"bbh_theoretical_power_15pct\": 0.88,\n707\t      \"math_theoretical_power_15pct\": 0.82,\n708\t      \"bbh_actual_power_15pct\": 0.85,\n709\t      \"math_actual_power_15pct\": 0.78,\n710\t      \"bbh_cohens_d_15pct\": -3.21,\n711\t      \"math_cohens_d_15pct\": -2.88,\n712\t      \"bbh_memorization_fraction\": 0.4,\n713\t      \"math_memorization_fraction\": 0.36,\n714\t      \"R2_with_new_benchmarks\": 0.968,\n715\t      \"bbh_dose_response_monotonic_theta_fixed\": true,\n716\t      \"math_dose_response_monotonic_theta_fixed\": true,\n717\t      \"bbh_theta_fixed_ratio\": 2.72,\n718\t      \"math_theta_fixed_ratio\": 2.58\n719\t    },\n720\t    \"tables\": [\n721\t      {\n722\t        \"name\": \"Table: Extended Power Function Validation\",\n723\t        \"columns\": [\n724\t          \"benchmark\",\n725\t          \"n_items\",\n726\t          \"theoretical_power_15pct\",\n727\t          \"actual_power_ctrl\",\n728\t          \"cohens_d_15pct\"\n729\t        ],\n730\t        \"rows\": [\n731\t          [\n732\t            \"MMLU\",\n733\t            14042,\n734\t            0.985,\n735\t            0.92,\n736\t            -3.95\n737\t          ],\n738\t          [\n739\t            \"HellaSwag\",\n740\t            10042,\n741\t            0.753,\n742\t            0.71,\n743\t            -2.64\n744\t          ],\n745\t          [\n746\t            \"BBH\",\n747\t            6511,\n748\t            0.88,\n749\t            0.85,\n750\t            -3.21\n751\t          ],\n752\t          [\n753\t            \"MATH\",\n754\t            5000,\n755\t            0.82,\n756\t            0.78,\n757\t            -2.88\n758\t          ],\n759\t          [\n760\t            \"GSM8K\",\n761\t            1319,\n762\t            0.59,\n763\t            0.55,\n764\t            -1.42\n765\t          ]\n766\t        ]\n767\t      }\n768\t    ],\n769\t    \"figures\": [],\n770\t    \"analysis\": \"BBH 和 MATH 的加入完善了 power function 的中间区段验证。5 个 benchmarks 覆盖了 1.3K 到 14K items 的完整范围，R²=0.968 确认 power 与 √n 的理论关系在实际 ctrl-contam 中成立。 这直接支撑 Claim 2 的核心论断：detection power is a predictable function of benchmark size。\\n\\n\\nBBH（6511 items）和 MATH（5000 items）填充了 GSM8K（1319）和 MMLU（14042）之间的 gap。 在 best 档下，两者都产生显著检测信号：BBH 因为 items 多且区分度高（BIG-Bench Hard 的 items 被设计为 challenging），theoretical power 接近 90%；MATH 的 items 更结构化（数学题）， memorization fraction 稍低（0.36 vs 0.40）因为数学题的 SFT 更容易产生 generalization 而非 verbatim memorization。两者的加入使 power function 的 R² 从 0.957 提升到 0.968， 进一步验证了 Claim 2 的 power ∝ f(n_items) 关系。这些中等规模 benchmarks 是实际应用中最常见的尺寸范围（多数 benchmarks 在 1K-10K 之间），因此验证至关重要。\\n\"\n771\t  },\n772\t  {\n773\t    \"name\": \"Natural Experiment (base→chat pairs)\",\n774\t    \"description\": \"v1 leaderboard base→chat model pairs 计算 Δlz* = lz*(chat) - lz*(base) 作为 SFT 效应代理。\\n\",\n775\t    \"results\": {\n776\t      \"n_pairs\": 21,\n777\t      \"n_complete_pairs\": 9,\n778\t      \"hellaswag_systematic_effect\": {\n779\t        \"mean_deviation\": -3.8,\n780\t        \"t_stat\": -4.2,\n781\t        \"p_value\": 0.0008,\n782\t        \"direction\": \"SFT decreases person-fit\"\n783\t      },\n784\t      \"gsm8k_systematic_effect\": {\n785\t        \"mean_deviation\": 4.5,\n786\t        \"t_stat\": 3.8,\n787\t        \"p_value\": 0.004,\n788\t        \"direction\": \"SFT increases person-fit\"\n789\t      },\n790\t      \"mmlu_effect\": {\n791\t        \"p_value\": 0.12,\n792\t        \"direction\": \"non-significant\"\n793\t      },\n794\t      \"arc_c_effect\": {\n795\t        \"p_value\": 0.31,\n796\t        \"direction\": \"non-significant\"\n797\t      },\n798\t      \"individual_outlier_pairs\": 1,\n799\t      \"outlier_model\": \"codellama-34b-instruct\",\n800\t      \"outlier_benchmark\": \"GSM8K\",\n801\t      \"outlier_delta_lz\": 8.7\n802\t    },\n803\t    \"tables\": [\n804\t      {\n805\t        \"name\": \"Table: Systematic SFT Effects on lz* (base→chat)\",\n806\t        \"columns\": [\n807\t          \"benchmark\",\n808\t          \"n_pairs\",\n809\t          \"mean_Δlz\",\n810\t          \"t_stat\",\n811\t          \"p_value\",\n812\t          \"interpretation\"\n813\t        ],\n814\t        \"rows\": [\n815\t          [\n816\t            \"HellaSwag\",\n817\t            9,\n818\t            -3.8,\n819\t            -4.2,\n820\t            0.0008,\n821\t            \"SFT improves commonsense (less aberrant)\"\n822\t          ],\n823\t          [\n824\t            \"GSM8K\",\n825\t            9,\n826\t            4.5,\n827\t            3.8,\n828\t            0.004,\n829\t            \"Math SFT creates new aberrance patterns\"\n830\t          ],\n831\t          [\n832\t            \"MMLU\",\n833\t            9,\n834\t            1.8,\n835\t            1.7,\n836\t            0.12,\n837\t            \"n.s.\"\n838\t          ],\n839\t          [\n840\t            \"ARC-C\",\n841\t            9,\n842\t            0.9,\n843\t            1.1,\n844\t            0.31,\n845\t            \"n.s.\"\n846\t          ]\n847\t        ]\n848\t      }\n849\t    ],\n850\t    \"figures\": [],\n851\t    \"analysis\": \"P2-optional 实验。提供了 real-world SFT 效应的 converging evidence，但受限于 a_r=0.111 的 discrimination failure。在 paper 中作为 supplementary finding 而非 primary evidence。\\n\\n\\nBest 档下 natural experiment 的结果比 registry 中的实际结果稍强：HellaSwag 和 GSM8K 显示更清晰的 systematic SFT effect（p<0.001 和 p<0.005），且出现一个 individual outlier （codellama-34b-instruct 在 GSM8K 上 Δlz*=8.7，远超 group mean）。这个 outlier 的出现是 best 档独有的——它提供了 \\\"自然实验中发现疑似污染\\\" 的 case study evidence。 HellaSwag 的 negative shift 解释：chat SFT 训练中包含了对话/常识推理数据， 这些与 HellaSwag 的 commonsense completion task 有 domain overlap，导致泛化性提升 但 pattern 变得 less aberrant（更符合 IRT 预测）。GSM8K positive shift： chat 模型的 math instruction tuning 不是 benchmark-specific memorization 而是 reasoning capability，但少数模型可能直接接触了 GSM8K items。 由于 a_r=0.111 的 discrimination failure，此实验只能作为 converging evidence，不是 primary claim。\\n\"\n852\t  },\n853\t  {\n854\t    \"name\": \"V1 IRT Refit Expanded (N=178)\",\n855\t    \"description\": \"扩大 v1 IRT 重拟合样本量至 N≥178，最终验证 Path D（large-scale audit）是否可行。\\n\",\n856\t    \"results\": {\n857\t      \"n_models\": 178,\n858\t      \"n_items\": 14042,\n859\t      \"3pl_a_pearson_r\": 0.13,\n860\t      \"2pl_a_pearson_r\": -0.03,\n861\t      \"3pl_b_pearson_r\": 0.66,\n862\t      \"a_r_below_threshold\": true,\n863\t      \"conclusion\": \"Path D confirmed dead. Classical MML-EM cannot recover IRT discrimination from LLM response data at available sample sizes.\"\n864\t    },\n865\t    \"tables\": [\n866\t      {\n867\t        \"name\": \"Table: IRT Parameter Recovery (Classical vs PSN-IRT)\",\n868\t        \"columns\": [\n869\t          \"method\",\n870\t          \"N_models\",\n871\t          \"a_pearson_r\",\n872\t          \"b_pearson_r\",\n873\t          \"conclusion\"\n874\t        ],\n875\t        \"rows\": [\n876\t          [\n877\t            \"MML-EM 3PL (N=63)\",\n878\t            63,\n879\t            0.111,\n880\t            0.626,\n881\t            \"a failure\"\n882\t          ],\n883\t          [\n884\t            \"MML-EM 3PL (N=178)\",\n885\t            178,\n886\t            0.13,\n887\t            0.66,\n888\t            \"a failure persists\"\n889\t          ],\n890\t          [\n891\t            \"PSN-IRT (neural)\",\n892\t            12,\n893\t            \"validated\",\n894\t            \"validated\",\n895\t            \"reference standard\"\n896\t          ]\n897\t        ]\n898\t      }\n899\t    ],\n900\t    \"figures\": [],\n901\t    \"analysis\": \"Path D 的确定性关闭是 paper structure 的关键节点。它确立了 \\\"why ctrl-contam, not leaderboard audit\\\" 的 methodological justification，并为 Future Work 中的 \\\"neural IRT at scale\\\" 提供了动机。\\n\\n\\n即使在 best 档，Path D（leaderboard-scale audit via classical IRT refit）仍然失败。 这不是 experiment failure 而是 honest negative result：classical IRT estimation 需要 hundreds of examinees with similar ability distributions，而 LLM response data 的特殊性（模型间 ability range 极大，item response 非 locally independent） 使得 MML-EM 无法恢复 discrimination parameters。a_r=0.13 << 0.4 threshold 确认 discriminability failure 不是样本量问题而是 structural incompatibility。 这本身是 Claim 3(c) 的贡献：quantifying the estimation challenge for neural IRT。\\n\"\n902\t  },\n903\t  {\n904\t    \"name\": \"4PL vs 3PL Ablation\",\n905\t    \"description\": \"4PL vs 3PL(d=1) 消融实验：量化 d 参数对检测灵敏度的影响。\\n\",\n906\t    \"results\": {\n907\t      \"mean_power_gain_4pl_vs_3pl\": {\n908\t        \"MMLU\": \"+28pp\",\n909\t        \"HellaSwag\": \"+27pp\",\n910\t        \"GSM8K\": \"+21pp\",\n911\t        \"ARC_C\": \"+15pp\",\n912\t        \"HumanEval\": \"+14pp\"\n913\t      },\n914\t      \"far_4pl\": 0.05,\n915\t      \"far_3pl\": \"0.05-0.17 (inflated)\",\n916\t      \"far_2pl\": \"0.50-1.00 (catastrophic)\",\n917\t      \"items_with_d_lt_095_mmlu\": \"46%\",\n918\t      \"ctrl_contam_4pl_d_15pct\": -3.95,\n919\t      \"ctrl_contam_3pl_d_15pct\": -1.82,\n920\t      \"power_loss_without_d\": \"54%\"\n921\t    },\n922\t    \"tables\": [\n923\t      {\n924\t        \"name\": \"Table: 4PL vs 3PL Detection Performance\",\n925\t        \"columns\": [\n926\t          \"benchmark\",\n927\t          \"n_items\",\n928\t          \"power_4pl_25pct\",\n929\t          \"power_3pl_25pct\",\n930\t          \"gain\",\n931\t          \"pct_items_d_lt_095\"\n932\t        ],\n933\t        \"rows\": [\n934\t          [\n935\t            \"MMLU\",\n936\t            14042,\n937\t            0.776,\n938\t            0.329,\n939\t            \"+44.7pp\",\n940\t            \"46%\"\n941\t          ],\n942\t          [\n943\t            \"HellaSwag\",\n944\t            10042,\n945\t            0.534,\n946\t            0.28,\n947\t            \"+25.4pp\",\n948\t            \"38%\"\n949\t          ],\n950\t          [\n951\t            \"GSM8K\",\n952\t            1319,\n953\t            0.73,\n954\t            0.334,\n955\t            \"+39.6pp\",\n956\t            \"42%\"\n957\t          ],\n958\t          [\n959\t            \"ARC-C\",\n960\t            295,\n961\t            0.132,\n962\t            0.091,\n963\t            \"+4.1pp\",\n964\t            \"29%\"\n965\t          ],\n966\t          [\n967\t            \"HumanEval\",\n968\t            164,\n969\t            0.318,\n970\t            0.165,\n971\t            \"+15.3pp\",\n972\t            \"35%\"\n973\t          ]\n974\t        ]\n975\t      }\n976\t    ],\n977\t    \"figures\": [],\n978\t    \"analysis\": \"4PL ablation 是 methodological rigor 的体现。Reviewer 可能质疑 \\\"为什么不用更简单的 3PL\\\"， 此实验给出定量答案：+28pp average power gain，54% signal loss without d。 结合 exp-4pl-real-data-degradation（r=0.225 between 4PL/3PL lz*）， establishes 4PL 作为 LLM person-fit 的 minimum viable parameterization。\\n\\n\\n4PL 的 d 参数（upper asymptote）对高能力 LLM 至关重要：当 d<1 时，P(correct) 的上限低于 1.0， 高能力模型在这些 items 上 \\\"应该\\\" 答错（按 4PL 预测）。如果忽略 d（设 d=1）， model 预测所有高能力模型都应该答对所有题——这会让 few errors 变成 extreme aberrance（false alarm）。 MMLU 46% items 有 d<0.95 意味着将近一半的题目有上限效应，忽略这些会产生巨大的 FAR 膨胀。 在 best 档下，ctrl-contam 进一步确认：同一污染实验用 3PL 分析时 |d| 从 3.95 降到 1.82， 因为 3PL 的 inflated null variance 稀释了真实信号。这证明 4PL 不是 \\\"nice-to-have\\\" 而是 LLM person-fit 分析的 necessary condition。\\n\"\n979\t  },\n980\t  {\n981\t    \"name\": \"Baseline Comparison — Accuracy Z-Score (completed)\",\n982\t    \"description\": \"Accuracy z-score 作为 same-level binary-only baseline 的扩展对比， 整合入完整 baseline comparison 实验中。\\n\",\n983\t    \"results\": {\n984\t      \"acc_zscore_auroc_5pct\": 0.55,\n985\t      \"acc_zscore_auroc_10pct\": 0.63,\n986\t      \"acc_zscore_auroc_15pct\": 0.71,\n987\t      \"acc_zscore_auroc_25pct\": 0.78,\n988\t      \"lz_star_advantage_over_zscore_5pct\": \"+0.23 AUROC\",\n989\t      \"lz_star_advantage_over_zscore_15pct\": \"+0.21 AUROC\",\n990\t      \"lz_star_advantage_over_zscore_25pct\": \"+0.16 AUROC\"\n991\t    },\n992\t    \"tables\": [],\n993\t    \"figures\": [],\n994\t    \"analysis\": \"Accuracy z-score 是 \\\"straw-man\\\" 但也是 fair comparison：它是唯一的 same-information-level baseline （binary only, no training data）。lz* 的 consistent +0.16-0.23 AUROC advantage 直接证明 IRT item parameters 提供了有价值的 structural information。\\n\\n\\nAccuracy z-score 只利用 total score（sum of binary responses）而丢失所有 item-level pattern information。lz* 的优势正来自于 item-level aberrance detection： 它区分 \\\"总分高因为答对了该对的题\\\" vs \\\"总分高因为答对了不该对的题\\\"。 在 5% 低污染时，只有 ~700 items（14042×5%）被 contaminate，total score change 微乎其微 （+2-3 pp accuracy），z-score 几乎无法检测。但 lz* 能捕捉到这 700 items 中的 \\\"不可能正确\\\" 模式。 这是 \\\"IRT structure as inductive bias\\\" 的最直接证明。\\n\"\n995\t  },\n996\t  {\n997\t    \"name\": \"Domain-Level Analysis\",\n998\t    \"description\": \"MMLU domain-level 分析：按 subject category 分别计算 person-fit，识别污染的 domain 分布。\\n\",\n999\t    \"results\": {\n1000\t      \"gemini_subjects_flagged\": \"50/57 (87.7%)\",\n1001\t      \"gemini_contamination_uniform\": true,\n1002\t      \"gemini_category_lz_range\": [\n1003\t        15.3,\n1004\t        21.2\n1005\t      ],\n1006\t      \"ctrl_contam_domain_uniformity\": \"uniform (as expected, since QLoRA trains on random 15% sample)\",\n1007\t      \"ctrl_contam_stem_lz\": 3.8,\n1008\t      \"ctrl_contam_humanities_lz\": 3.3,\n1009\t      \"ctrl_contam_social_sci_lz\": 3.5,\n1010\t      \"ctrl_contam_other_lz\": 3.2,\n1011\t      \"doubao_selective_domains\": true,\n1012\t      \"doubao_negative_pattern\": \"STEM and Humanities strongly negative, Other positive\"\n1013\t    },\n1014\t    \"tables\": [\n1015\t      {\n1016\t        \"name\": \"Table: MMLU Domain-Level lz* (Gemini-1.5 vs Ctrl-Contam)\",\n1017\t        \"columns\": [\n1018\t          \"domain\",\n1019\t          \"gemini_lz\",\n1020\t          \"ctrl_contam_15_lz\",\n1021\t          \"ctrl_contam_clean_lz\"\n1022\t        ],\n1023\t        \"rows\": [\n1024\t          [\n1025\t            \"STEM\",\n1026\t            21.2,\n1027\t            3.8,\n1028\t            0.1\n1029\t          ],\n1030\t          [\n1031\t            \"Humanities\",\n1032\t            17.9,\n1033\t            3.3,\n1034\t            -0.2\n1035\t          ],\n1036\t          [\n1037\t            \"Social Sciences\",\n1038\t            15.9,\n1039\t            3.5,\n1040\t            0.0\n1041\t          ],\n1042\t          [\n1043\t            \"Other\",\n1044\t            15.3,\n1045\t            3.2,\n1046\t            0.1\n1047\t          ]\n1048\t        ]\n1049\t      }\n1050\t    ],\n1051\t    \"figures\": [],\n1052\t    \"analysis\": \"Domain analysis 提供了 contamination 的 \\\"spatial resolution\\\"：从 aggregate model-level detection 到 domain-level localization。在 paper 中服务于两个目的：(a) 验证 ctrl-contam 内部一致性 （random sampling → uniform signal），(b) case study 中展示不同 contamination type 的 domain fingerprint。\\n\\n\\nDomain analysis 在 best 档下产生两个 clear findings：(1) Gemini-1.5 的 contamination 是 uniform across domains（所有 subject 都被 memorize），consistent with \\\"bulk training data leak\\\" 而非 \\\"selective domain tuning\\\"；(2) ctrl-contam 模型的 domain-level signal 也是 uniform （因为 QLoRA 训练样本是 randomly sampled across all subjects），验证了实验设计的 internal consistency。 Doubao 的 selective negative pattern 则展示了不同类型的 anomaly：可能是 domain-specific training data 导致某些 domains 泛化过强（lz*<0 = over-consistent pattern）。\\n\"\n1053\t  },\n1054\t  {\n1055\t    \"name\": \"Leaderboard Audit (Abandoned)\",\n1056\t    \"description\": \"Open LLM Leaderboard v1 大规模 13K+ 模型扫描。因 IRT refit failure 放弃。\\n\",\n1057\t    \"results\": {\n1058\t      \"status\": \"ABANDONED\",\n1059\t      \"reason\": \"a_r=0.111 discrimination failure makes lz* degenerate to accuracy-like metric at scale\",\n1060\t      \"paper_treatment\": \"Data availability noted in Discussion/Future Work; 13K+ per-item data available for future neural IRT estimation\"\n1061\t    },\n1062\t    \"tables\": [],\n1063\t    \"figures\": [],\n1064\t    \"analysis\": \"ABANDONED。在 paper 中转化为 methodological contribution：量化了 classical vs neural IRT 在 LLM context 中的 gap，为 future work 提供了 concrete roadmap（13K+ data available, awaiting better estimation methods）。\\n\\n即使在 best 档，leaderboard audit 仍然 abandoned。这不影响 best 档的叙事， 因为 ctrl-contam 提供了比 leaderboard audit 更强的 ground-truth validation。 Audit 的 abandonment 本身是 honest negative result (Claim 3c)：classical IRT 的 sample size requirement 与 LLM evaluation ecosystem 不兼容。 Paper 中将其定位为 \\\"future work when neural IRT estimation at scale becomes feasible\\\"。\\n\"\n1065\t  }\n1066\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f4e042fb-0a90-4bbe-8eb1-3013bf130d8d","uuid":"550107b1-adb0-470b-ac14-3fc799784a5d","timestamp":"2026-05-20T19:22:28.208Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0519-3/projects/irt_personfit_contam/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260520T190245/best/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Controlled Contamination Pilot (Qwen3.5-9B)\",\n    \"description\": \"Qwen3.5-9B × 4 conditions (0%-seed1/0%-seed2/15%/50%) × MMLU。 验证 Δlz* 显著性、clean-vs-clean noise floor、seen/unseen memorization fraction。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"clean_s1_lz_star\": 7.2,\n      \"clean_s2_lz_star\": 6.8,\n      \"clean_delta_lz\": 0.4,\n      \"clean_delta_nonsig\": true,\n      \"contam_15_lz_star_free\": 2.8,\n      \"contam_15_delta_lz_free\": -4.1,\n      \"contam_15_cohens_d\": -3.95,\n      \"contam_50_lz_star_free\": 4.9,\n      \"contam_50_delta_lz_free\": -2.0,\n      \"contam_15_lz_star_fixed\": 10.5,\n      \"contam_50_lz_star_fixed\": 16.8,\n      \"theta_fixed_delta_15\": 3.5,\n      \"theta_fixed_delta_50\": 9.8,\n      \"theta_fixed_ratio\": 2.8,\n      \"accuracy_clean\": 0.71,\n      \"accuracy_contam_15\": 0.76,\n      \"accuracy_contam_50\": 0.8,\n      \"accuracy_contam_15_seen\": 0.86,\n      \"accuracy_contam_15_unseen\": 0.73,\n      \"memorization_fraction_15\": 0.42,\n      \"memorization_fraction_50\": 0.31,\n      \"theta_shift_clean\": -0.08,\n      \"theta_shift_contam_15\": 0.22,\n      \"theta_shift_contam_50\": 0.41\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Qwen3.5-9B Pilot Results\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"condition\",\n          \"accuracy\",\n          \"lz_star_free\",\n          \"lz_star_fixed\",\n          \"theta_MLE\",\n          \"delta_lz_free\",\n          \"delta_lz_fixed\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"clean_s1\",\n            0.71,\n            7.2,\n            7.2,\n            -0.08,\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"clean_s2\",\n            0.71,\n            6.8,\n            6.8,\n            -0.09,\n            0.4,\n            0.4\n          ],\n          [\n            \"contam_15\",\n            0.76,\n            2.8,\n            10.5,\n            0.22,\n            -4.1,\n            3.5\n          ],\n          [\n            \"contam_50\",\n            0.8,\n            4.9,\n            16.8,\n            0.41,\n            -2.0,\n            9.8\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Go/no-go 信号明确通过。|d|=3.95 远超 0.8 的 large effect 阈值。θ-fixed 恢复单调 dose-response (ratio=2.80∈[2.5,4.0])，确认 θ-shift 是唯一导致 free-θ 非单调的机制。 memorization_fraction=0.42 意味着理论 power 的 ~42% 可在实际中实现——MMLU 15% 理论 power 98.5% × 0.42 = adjusted power ≈41%，但 lz* 检测的是 aggregate pattern 而非逐 item 检测， 所以 aggregate Δlz* 仍然产生 |d|≈4 的强效应。\\n\\n\\nQwen3.5-9B 作为较新架构（含 thinking 能力），SFT memorization 效率略高于 Qwen2.5-7B。 15% 污染产生强信号（|d|≈4.0）是因为 QLoRA 在小比例 seen items 上产生明确的 aberrant pattern： 模型在高难度 seen items 上异常正确，而在 unseen items 上保持原有错误模式。memorization_fraction≈0.42 说明 ~42% 的 seen items 被完全记忆（产生 aberrant response），剩余 58% 产生了泛化而非逐字记忆。 θ-shift 机制与 pilot 一致：污染提升整体能力估计，θ_MLE 上升吸收了部分 aberrance signal， θ-fixed 恢复单调性。clean-vs-clean Δ≈0.4 确认 noise floor 远低于检测阈值。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Full Multi-Model Controlled Contamination\",\n    \"description\": \"4 模型 (Qwen3.5-9B, Gemma-4-31B, Llama-3.1-8B, Mistral-7B-v0.3) × 6 contamination levels (0/5/10/15/25/50%) × 3 benchmarks (MMLU, GSM8K, HellaSwag)。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"cohens_d_15pct_mmlu\": {\n        \"qwen3.5-9b\": -3.95,\n        \"gemma-4-31b\": -4.52,\n        \"llama-3.1-8b\": -2.85,\n        \"mistral-7b-v0.3\": -2.42\n      },\n      \"cohens_d_15pct_mean\": 3.44,\n      \"cohens_d_15pct_min\": 2.42,\n      \"models_significant_at_15pct\": 4,\n      \"benchmarks_significant_per_model\": {\n        \"qwen3.5-9b\": 3,\n        \"gemma-4-31b\": 3,\n        \"llama-3.1-8b\": 2,\n        \"mistral-7b-v0.3\": 2\n      },\n      \"gsm8k_cohens_d_15pct\": {\n        \"qwen3.5-9b\": -1.42,\n        \"gemma-4-31b\": -1.68,\n        \"llama-3.1-8b\": -0.91,\n        \"mistral-7b-v0.3\": -0.85\n      },\n      \"gsm8k_all_above_0.8\": true,\n      \"memorization_fraction_15pct\": {\n        \"qwen3.5-9b\": 0.42,\n        \"gemma-4-31b\": 0.48,\n        \"llama-3.1-8b\": 0.35,\n        \"mistral-7b-v0.3\": 0.33\n      },\n      \"memorization_fraction_mean\": 0.4,\n      \"theta_fixed_dose_response_ratio\": {\n        \"qwen3.5-9b\": 2.8,\n        \"gemma-4-31b\": 3.45,\n        \"llama-3.1-8b\": 2.62,\n        \"mistral-7b-v0.3\": 2.55\n      },\n      \"theta_fixed_ratio_mean\": 2.86,\n      \"theta_fixed_all_monotonic\": true,\n      \"seen_unseen_lz_gap_15pct\": {\n        \"qwen3.5-9b\": 3.2,\n        \"gemma-4-31b\": 4.1,\n        \"llama-3.1-8b\": 2.7,\n        \"mistral-7b-v0.3\": 2.5\n      },\n      \"seen_unseen_gap_mean\": 3.13,\n      \"dose_response_mmlu_theta_fixed\": {\n        \"5pct\": {\n          \"qwen\": 1.1,\n          \"gemma\": 1.4,\n          \"llama\": 0.8,\n          \"mistral\": 0.7\n        },\n        \"10pct\": {\n          \"qwen\": 2.2,\n          \"gemma\": 2.7,\n          \"llama\": 1.6,\n          \"mistral\": 1.4\n        },\n        \"15pct\": {\n          \"qwen\": 3.5,\n          \"gemma\": 4.2,\n          \"llama\": 2.5,\n          \"mistral\": 2.2\n        },\n        \"25pct\": {\n          \"qwen\": 5.8,\n          \"gemma\": 7.0,\n          \"llama\": 4.1,\n          \"mistral\": 3.7\n        },\n        \"50pct\": {\n          \"qwen\": 9.8,\n          \"gemma\": 14.5,\n          \"llama\": 6.6,\n          \"mistral\": 6.3\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Cross-Model Detection at 15% Contamination (MMLU)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"model\",\n          \"accuracy_clean\",\n          \"accuracy_contam15\",\n          \"delta_lz_free\",\n          \"delta_lz_fixed\",\n          \"cohens_d\",\n          \"memorization_frac\",\n          \"theta_shift\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Qwen3.5-9B\",\n            0.71,\n            0.76,\n            -4.1,\n            3.5,\n            -3.95,\n            0.42,\n            0.3\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Gemma-4-31B\",\n            0.78,\n            0.84,\n            -4.8,\n            4.2,\n            -4.52,\n            0.48,\n            0.35\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Llama-3.1-8B\",\n            0.63,\n            0.69,\n            -2.9,\n            2.5,\n            -2.85,\n            0.35,\n            0.24\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Mistral-7B-v0.3\",\n            0.61,\n            0.67,\n            -2.5,\n            2.2,\n            -2.42,\n            0.33,\n            0.21\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: GSM8K Small-Benchmark Detection at 15%\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"model\",\n          \"n_items\",\n          \"delta_lz_fixed\",\n          \"cohens_d\",\n          \"significant_p005\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Qwen3.5-9B\",\n            1319,\n            1.8,\n            -1.42,\n            true\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Gemma-4-31B\",\n            1319,\n            2.1,\n            -1.68,\n            true\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Llama-3.1-8B\",\n            1319,\n            1.2,\n            -0.91,\n            true\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Mistral-7B-v0.3\",\n            1319,\n            1.1,\n            -0.85,\n            true\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: θ-Fixed Dose-Response (MMLU, all models)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"contam_level\",\n          \"qwen_delta\",\n          \"gemma_delta\",\n          \"llama_delta\",\n          \"mistral_delta\",\n          \"monotonic\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"5%\",\n            1.1,\n            1.4,\n            0.8,\n            0.7,\n            \"✓\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"10%\",\n            2.2,\n            2.7,\n            1.6,\n            1.4,\n            \"✓\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"15%\",\n            3.5,\n            4.2,\n            2.5,\n            2.2,\n            \"✓\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"25%\",\n            5.8,\n            7.0,\n            4.1,\n            3.7,\n            \"✓\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"50%\",\n            9.8,\n            14.5,\n            6.6,\n            6.3,\n            \"✓\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"核心假设 1 完全验证：SFT memorization fingerprint 跨 4 个模型家族一致。效应量范围 [2.42, 4.52] 远超统计显著性需求。θ-fixed 策略普适性确认（假设 2），所有模型的 dose-response ratio ∈[2.55, 3.45]。 GSM8K 的小 benchmark 假设（假设 4）通过 |d|>0.8 验证，尽管绝对信号弱于 MMLU（n=14042 vs 1319）， paired comparison 设计弥补了 power 不足。这为 Claim 1 提供了跨架构、跨规模的 ground-truth validation。\\n\\n\\nBest 档要求 4/4 模型在 15% 均显著。Gemma-4-31B 作为 31B 参数模型具有更强的 memorization 能力 （SFT 时容量更大，更容易逐字存储 seen items），因此 |d| 最高（4.52）且 memorization_fraction 最高（0.48）。Llama-3.1-8B 和 Mistral-7B-v0.3 参数较少但仍在 |d|>2.0 范围，因为 QLoRA 即使在小模型上也能有效注入 memorization——关键是 LoRA rank 足够捕获 item-level patterns。 GSM8K 虽然只有 ~1.3K items（理论 power 较低），但 ctrl-contam 测量的是 Δlz*（within-model shift） 而非绝对检测，所以即使 power function 预测 single-model detection 只有 59%， paired comparison 的效应量仍可达 |d|>0.8。θ-fixed 策略在所有模型上普适是因为 θ-shift 机制是 IRT MLE 估计的数学性质（污染→更多正确→θ_MLE↑），与模型架构无关。 Seen/unseen gap∈[2.5,5.0] 反映了 SFT 的部分泛化效应：seen items lz*≈0（memorized items 看起来\\\"正常\\\"），unseen items lz* 保持高值（未被 memorize 的 items 仍然产生 aberrant patterns）。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Baseline Comparison (≥5 methods)\",\n    \"description\": \"在 ctrl-contam ground-truth 上比较 IRT-FIT vs 5+ baselines 的 AUROC。 Baselines: ConStat (re-test), Min-K%++ (token probs), accuracy z-score, PPL-based detection, random baseline, + ML classifiers (LR/RF)。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"auroc_5pct\": {\n        \"lz_star_theta_fixed\": 0.78,\n        \"lr_binary_oracle\": 0.62,\n        \"rf_binary_oracle\": 0.59,\n        \"accuracy_zscore\": 0.55,\n        \"min_k_pp\": 0.71,\n        \"ppl_based\": 0.68,\n        \"constat_retest\": 0.65,\n        \"random\": 0.5\n      },\n      \"auroc_10pct\": {\n        \"lz_star_theta_fixed\": 0.87,\n        \"lr_binary_oracle\": 0.74,\n        \"rf_binary_oracle\": 0.72,\n        \"accuracy_zscore\": 0.63,\n        \"min_k_pp\": 0.82,\n        \"ppl_based\": 0.79,\n        \"constat_retest\": 0.76,\n        \"random\": 0.5\n      },\n      \"auroc_15pct\": {\n        \"lz_star_theta_fixed\": 0.92,\n        \"lr_binary_oracle\": 0.84,\n        \"rf_binary_oracle\": 0.82,\n        \"accuracy_zscore\": 0.71,\n        \"min_k_pp\": 0.89,\n        \"ppl_based\": 0.86,\n        \"constat_retest\": 0.83,\n        \"random\": 0.5\n      },\n      \"auroc_25pct\": {\n        \"lz_star_theta_fixed\": 0.94,\n        \"lr_binary_oracle\": 0.92,\n        \"rf_binary_oracle\": 0.91,\n        \"accuracy_zscore\": 0.78,\n        \"min_k_pp\": 0.95,\n        \"ppl_based\": 0.93,\n        \"constat_retest\": 0.91,\n        \"random\": 0.5\n      },\n      \"lz_minus_best_baseline_5pct\": 0.07,\n      \"lz_minus_best_binary_baseline_5pct\": 0.16,\n      \"crossover_point\": \"~20% (Min-K%++ surpasses lz* above 20%)\",\n      \"bootstrap_ci_width_mean\": 0.04,\n      \"information_levels\": {\n        \"binary_only\": [\n          \"lz_star\",\n          \"accuracy_zscore\",\n          \"lr_binary\",\n          \"rf_binary\"\n        ],\n        \"token_probs\": [\n          \"min_k_pp\",\n          \"ppl_based\"\n        ],\n        \"retest_required\": [\n          \"constat_retest\"\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: AUROC Comparison Across Contamination Levels (MMLU, averaged over 4 models)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"method\",\n          \"info_level\",\n          \"auroc_5pct\",\n          \"auroc_10pct\",\n          \"auroc_15pct\",\n          \"auroc_25pct\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"lz*_θ-fixed\",\n            \"binary\",\n            \"0.78±0.03\",\n            \"0.87±0.03\",\n            \"0.92±0.02\",\n            \"0.94±0.02\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Min-K%++\",\n            \"token_probs\",\n            \"0.71±0.04\",\n            \"0.82±0.03\",\n            \"0.89±0.02\",\n            \"0.95±0.01\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"PPL-based\",\n            \"log_probs\",\n            \"0.68±0.04\",\n            \"0.79±0.03\",\n            \"0.86±0.03\",\n            \"0.93±0.02\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ConStat\",\n            \"retest\",\n            \"0.65±0.05\",\n            \"0.76±0.04\",\n            \"0.83±0.03\",\n            \"0.91±0.02\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"LR (oracle)\",\n            \"binary\",\n            \"0.62±0.05\",\n            \"0.74±0.04\",\n            \"0.84±0.03\",\n            \"0.92±0.02\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"RF (oracle)\",\n            \"binary\",\n            \"0.59±0.06\",\n            \"0.72±0.04\",\n            \"0.82±0.03\",\n            \"0.91±0.02\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Acc z-score\",\n            \"binary\",\n            \"0.55±0.05\",\n            \"0.63±0.04\",\n            \"0.71±0.04\",\n            \"0.78±0.03\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Random\",\n            \"—\",\n            0.5,\n            0.5,\n            0.5,\n            0.5\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: lz* Advantage Over Best Baseline at Each Level\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"contam_level\",\n          \"best_baseline\",\n          \"best_baseline_auroc\",\n          \"lz_auroc\",\n          \"delta\",\n          \"significant\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"5%\",\n            \"Min-K%++\",\n            0.71,\n            0.78,\n            0.07,\n            \"p<0.05\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"10%\",\n            \"Min-K%++\",\n            0.82,\n            0.87,\n            0.05,\n            \"p<0.05\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"15%\",\n            \"Min-K%++\",\n            0.89,\n            0.92,\n            0.03,\n            \"p=0.08\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"25%\",\n            \"Min-K%++\",\n            0.95,\n            0.94,\n            -0.01,\n            \"n.s.\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Best 档的 headline result：lz* 在实际关键的 5-10% 低污染率下无需任何标注数据或 token access 即胜过 supervised baselines 和 token-level methods。这验证了 IRT structure 作为 inductive bias 在 data-scarce regime 的优势。crossover 发生在 ~20%——高于此水平时 Min-K%++ 的 token-level signal 更强，但 20%+ 的污染在实际场景中已经很容易被 accuracy jump 发现。 关键 framing：lz* 在 \\\"检测困难\\\" 的低污染区间胜出，正是 minimal-information 方法最有价值的 regime。\\n\\n\\nlz* 在 5-10% 低污染率胜出所有 baselines（假设 5）的机制：IRT 结构作为 inductive bias。 在低污染率下，signal-to-noise 极低——只有 5-10% 的 items 携带 contamination signal。 ML classifiers（LR/RF）即使有 oracle labels 也面临严重的 class imbalance（5% positive）， 且 binary feature space（0/1 per item）在低 contamination 时几乎不可分。 lz* 的优势来自 IRT model 提供的 structured expectation：它知道每个 item 的 expected P(correct|θ)， 因此即使只有 5% items 被 contaminate，这些 items 上的 \\\"impossible correctness\\\"（高难度 item 被答对） 会被精确捕获为 aberrance。而 ML classifier 只看到 raw 0/1 pattern，缺乏 item difficulty 的先验。 Min-K%++ 在 5% 时 AUROC=0.71 弱于 lz*（0.78）是因为 token-level 信号在极低污染时被 noise 淹没， 但在 20%+ 时 token distribution shift 变得明显，超过 binary-level detection。 accuracy z-score 作为 same-level binary baseline 在所有水平都远不如 lz*—— 它只看 total score 而非 pattern，丢失了 item-level aberrance 信息。 这确立了 IRT structure 作为 binary-only 方法的关键 advantage。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Post-RL Signal Retention\",\n    \"description\": \"Qwen3.5-9B 上先 SFT 污染（15%）再 GRPO 训练，测试 Δlz* 在 RL 后是否保持。 回应 Wang et al. (2025) 的 MIA 全失效发现。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"pre_rl_delta_lz_fixed\": 3.5,\n      \"pre_rl_cohens_d\": -3.95,\n      \"pre_rl_accuracy_contam\": 0.76,\n      \"pre_rl_accuracy_seen\": 0.86,\n      \"post_rl_delta_lz_fixed\": 2.8,\n      \"post_rl_cohens_d\": -3.15,\n      \"post_rl_accuracy_contam\": 0.79,\n      \"post_rl_accuracy_seen\": 0.82,\n      \"signal_retention\": 0.8,\n      \"retention_above_70pct\": true,\n      \"min_k_pp_pre_rl_auroc\": 0.89,\n      \"min_k_pp_post_rl_auroc\": 0.54,\n      \"ppl_pre_rl_auroc\": 0.86,\n      \"ppl_post_rl_auroc\": 0.52,\n      \"lz_star_pre_rl_auroc\": 0.92,\n      \"lz_star_post_rl_auroc\": 0.85,\n      \"seen_accuracy_drop_post_rl\": 0.04,\n      \"unseen_accuracy_gain_post_rl\": 0.03,\n      \"memorization_fraction_post_rl\": 0.34,\n      \"theta_shift_post_rl\": 0.28\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Pre-RL vs Post-RL Detection Comparison\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"method\",\n          \"info_level\",\n          \"auroc_pre_rl\",\n          \"auroc_post_rl\",\n          \"retention_pct\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"lz*_θ-fixed\",\n            \"binary\",\n            0.92,\n            0.85,\n            \"80%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Min-K%++\",\n            \"token_probs\",\n            0.89,\n            0.54,\n            \"4%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"PPL-based\",\n            \"log_probs\",\n            0.86,\n            0.52,\n            \"2%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Acc z-score\",\n            \"binary\",\n            0.71,\n            0.65,\n            \"60%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"LR (oracle)\",\n            \"binary\",\n            0.84,\n            0.72,\n            \"56%\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Binary Response Patterns Pre/Post RL\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"metric\",\n          \"pre_rl\",\n          \"post_rl\",\n          \"change\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Δlz*_fixed\",\n            3.5,\n            2.8,\n            \"-20%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Cohen's d\",\n            -3.95,\n            -3.15,\n            \"-20%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Seen accuracy\",\n            0.86,\n            0.82,\n            \"-4pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Unseen accuracy\",\n            0.73,\n            0.76,\n            \"+3pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Memorization fraction\",\n            0.42,\n            0.34,\n            \"-8pp\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"这是论文最强的 selling point 之一。Wang et al. (2025) 证明所有 10 种 log-prob based methods 在 RL 后降至 random，而 lz* 保留 80% 信号。这直接证明了 minimal-information operating point 的 structural advantage：binary patterns 对 RL 是 robust 的，因为 RL 优化的是 generation quality 而非 item-level correctness erasure。paper 可以引用此结果 直接回应 Wang et al. 的 \\\"all methods fail\\\" claim——\\\"all TOKEN-LEVEL methods fail, but BINARY-LEVEL detection survives.\\\"\\n\\n\\nPost-RL signal retention ≥70%（假设 3）成立的核心原因：GRPO 优化的是 reward signal（正确率/格式）， 而非 item-level response distribution。SFT memorization 写入的是 \\\"看到 item X → 输出 answer Y\\\" 的 pattern，这是 parameter-level 的 association。GRPO 的 policy gradient 更新主要影响 reasoning chain 的 token distribution，而 binary correctness 层面的 memorization 痕迹 （hard item 仍然答对）大部分保留。signal 从 3.5 降到 2.8（retention=80%）的 20% 损失来自： (a) RL 训练中少量 seen items 的 memorization 被 \\\"覆盖\\\"（RL 发现了不同的 reasoning path）， (b) RL 普遍提升了 unseen items 的正确率（θ进一步上升），轻微压缩了 seen/unseen gap。 但关键是 binary response 层面的 aberrant pattern 仍然存在——模型在 \\\"不该答对\\\" 的 hard items 上 仍然答对，这个 pattern-level signal 是 RL 无法消除的，因为 RL 没有动机去 \\\"故意答错\\\" 已经答对的题。 相比之下，MIA methods（Min-K%++, PPL）失效是因为 RL 彻底重塑了 token-level distribution—— reasoning tokens 的 perplexity 分布被 GRPO 重新优化，训练数据的 token-level fingerprint 消失。 这是 binary vs token-level detection 的 structural advantage。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Multiscale lzm Statistic\",\n    \"description\": \"实现 Hong, Lin & Cheng (2021) 的 multiscale lzm——跨 benchmark 聚合的标准化 lz* 总分。 在 PSN-IRT 12 模型和 ctrl-contam 模型上验证。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"gemini15_lzm\": 42.8,\n      \"deepseek_v3_lzm\": 38.2,\n      \"yi_lightning_lzm\": 35.6,\n      \"qwen_plus_lzm\": 33.1,\n      \"doubao_pro_lzm\": -8.4,\n      \"mistral_7b_lzm\": 2.1,\n      \"lzm_vs_mean_lz_correlation\": 0.97,\n      \"lzm_flagged_at_alpha005\": \"11/12\",\n      \"ctrl_contam_lzm_clean\": 8.5,\n      \"ctrl_contam_lzm_15pct\": 14.2,\n      \"ctrl_contam_lzm_50pct\": 22.8,\n      \"lzm_cohens_d_15pct\": -4.12,\n      \"lzm_incremental_over_single_benchmark\": \"+0.15 AUROC vs single-best benchmark\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: lzm Scores for PSN-IRT 12 Models\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"model\",\n          \"lz_mmlu\",\n          \"lz_hellaswag\",\n          \"lz_gsm8k\",\n          \"lz_arc_c\",\n          \"lz_humaneval\",\n          \"lzm_aggregate\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Gemini-1.5\",\n            31.8,\n            28.4,\n            12.1,\n            6.2,\n            -2.4,\n            42.8\n          ],\n          [\n            \"DeepSeek-V3\",\n            28.6,\n            25.1,\n            10.8,\n            5.8,\n            -1.2,\n            38.2\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Yi-Lightning\",\n            26.4,\n            22.3,\n            9.5,\n            -0.3,\n            -1.8,\n            35.6\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Doubao-Pro\",\n            -12.5,\n            -8.2,\n            4.3,\n            -2.1,\n            -3.8,\n            -8.4\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"lzm 提供了一个 principled 的跨 benchmark 聚合方式，比简单 mean(lz*) 有理论优势 （proper variance weighting）。在 ctrl-contam 中，multi-benchmark contamination 的 lzm 检测力比 single-best benchmark 强 0.15 AUROC，证明了 multiscale 方法的实用价值。 但核心贡献仍是 per-benchmark lz*，lzm 作为 extension/robustness check。\\n\\n\\nlzm 聚合跨 benchmark 信号的原理：如果一个模型在多个 benchmarks 上都表现异常， lzm 将这些独立 signals 标准化后求和，产生比任何单一 benchmark 更强的检测统计量。 在 best 档下，ctrl-contam 跨 3 个 benchmarks 都注入了污染，lzm 的 multi-benchmark aggregation 产生额外的 +0.15 AUROC 增益。对 PSN-IRT 12 模型，lzm 与 mean_lz* 高度相关（r=0.97） 因为大多数模型的 anomaly 在所有 benchmarks 上方向一致（positive direction dominant, 93.3% cells）。 Doubao-pro 的负 lzm 反映其独特的 negative lz* 模式（STEM 和 Humanities domains 特异性不足）。 这是一个 methodological addition（不是核心贡献），但增强了 paper 的 completeness。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Extra Benchmarks (BBH + MATH)\",\n    \"description\": \"BBH (6,511 items) 和 MATH (5,000 items) 扩展，填充 1K-10K items 的 power gap。 在 ctrl-contam 模型上验证中等规模 benchmark 的检测力。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"bbh_theoretical_power_15pct\": 0.88,\n      \"math_theoretical_power_15pct\": 0.82,\n      \"bbh_actual_power_15pct\": 0.85,\n      \"math_actual_power_15pct\": 0.78,\n      \"bbh_cohens_d_15pct\": -3.21,\n      \"math_cohens_d_15pct\": -2.88,\n      \"bbh_memorization_fraction\": 0.4,\n      \"math_memorization_fraction\": 0.36,\n      \"R2_with_new_benchmarks\": 0.968,\n      \"bbh_dose_response_monotonic_theta_fixed\": true,\n      \"math_dose_response_monotonic_theta_fixed\": true,\n      \"bbh_theta_fixed_ratio\": 2.72,\n      \"math_theta_fixed_ratio\": 2.58\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Extended Power Function Validation\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"benchmark\",\n          \"n_items\",\n          \"theoretical_power_15pct\",\n          \"actual_power_ctrl\",\n          \"cohens_d_15pct\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"MMLU\",\n            14042,\n            0.985,\n            0.92,\n            -3.95\n          ],\n          [\n            \"HellaSwag\",\n            10042,\n            0.753,\n            0.71,\n            -2.64\n          ],\n          [\n            \"BBH\",\n            6511,\n            0.88,\n            0.85,\n            -3.21\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MATH\",\n            5000,\n            0.82,\n            0.78,\n            -2.88\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GSM8K\",\n            1319,\n            0.59,\n            0.55,\n            -1.42\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"BBH 和 MATH 的加入完善了 power function 的中间区段验证。5 个 benchmarks 覆盖了 1.3K 到 14K items 的完整范围，R²=0.968 确认 power 与 √n 的理论关系在实际 ctrl-contam 中成立。 这直接支撑 Claim 2 的核心论断：detection power is a predictable function of benchmark size。\\n\\n\\nBBH（6511 items）和 MATH（5000 items）填充了 GSM8K（1319）和 MMLU（14042）之间的 gap。 在 best 档下，两者都产生显著检测信号：BBH 因为 items 多且区分度高（BIG-Bench Hard 的 items 被设计为 challenging），theoretical power 接近 90%；MATH 的 items 更结构化（数学题）， memorization fraction 稍低（0.36 vs 0.40）因为数学题的 SFT 更容易产生 generalization 而非 verbatim memorization。两者的加入使 power function 的 R² 从 0.957 提升到 0.968， 进一步验证了 Claim 2 的 power ∝ f(n_items) 关系。这些中等规模 benchmarks 是实际应用中最常见的尺寸范围（多数 benchmarks 在 1K-10K 之间），因此验证至关重要。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Natural Experiment (base→chat pairs)\",\n    \"description\": \"v1 leaderboard base→chat model pairs 计算 Δlz* = lz*(chat) - lz*(base) 作为 SFT 效应代理。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_pairs\": 21,\n      \"n_complete_pairs\": 9,\n      \"hellaswag_systematic_effect\": {\n        \"mean_deviation\": -3.8,\n        \"t_stat\": -4.2,\n        \"p_value\": 0.0008,\n        \"direction\": \"SFT decreases person-fit\"\n      },\n      \"gsm8k_systematic_effect\": {\n        \"mean_deviation\": 4.5,\n        \"t_stat\": 3.8,\n        \"p_value\": 0.004,\n        \"direction\": \"SFT increases person-fit\"\n      },\n      \"mmlu_effect\": {\n        \"p_value\": 0.12,\n        \"direction\": \"non-significant\"\n      },\n      \"arc_c_effect\": {\n        \"p_value\": 0.31,\n        \"direction\": \"non-significant\"\n      },\n      \"individual_outlier_pairs\": 1,\n      \"outlier_model\": \"codellama-34b-instruct\",\n      \"outlier_benchmark\": \"GSM8K\",\n      \"outlier_delta_lz\": 8.7\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Systematic SFT Effects on lz* (base→chat)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"benchmark\",\n          \"n_pairs\",\n          \"mean_Δlz\",\n          \"t_stat\",\n          \"p_value\",\n          \"interpretation\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"HellaSwag\",\n            9,\n            -3.8,\n            -4.2,\n            0.0008,\n            \"SFT improves commonsense (less aberrant)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GSM8K\",\n            9,\n            4.5,\n            3.8,\n            0.004,\n            \"Math SFT creates new aberrance patterns\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MMLU\",\n            9,\n            1.8,\n            1.7,\n            0.12,\n            \"n.s.\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC-C\",\n            9,\n            0.9,\n            1.1,\n            0.31,\n            \"n.s.\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"P2-optional 实验。提供了 real-world SFT 效应的 converging evidence，但受限于 a_r=0.111 的 discrimination failure。在 paper 中作为 supplementary finding 而非 primary evidence。\\n\\n\\nBest 档下 natural experiment 的结果比 registry 中的实际结果稍强：HellaSwag 和 GSM8K 显示更清晰的 systematic SFT effect（p<0.001 和 p<0.005），且出现一个 individual outlier （codellama-34b-instruct 在 GSM8K 上 Δlz*=8.7，远超 group mean）。这个 outlier 的出现是 best 档独有的——它提供了 \\\"自然实验中发现疑似污染\\\" 的 case study evidence。 HellaSwag 的 negative shift 解释：chat SFT 训练中包含了对话/常识推理数据， 这些与 HellaSwag 的 commonsense completion task 有 domain overlap，导致泛化性提升 但 pattern 变得 less aberrant（更符合 IRT 预测）。GSM8K positive shift： chat 模型的 math instruction tuning 不是 benchmark-specific memorization 而是 reasoning capability，但少数模型可能直接接触了 GSM8K items。 由于 a_r=0.111 的 discrimination failure，此实验只能作为 converging evidence，不是 primary claim。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"V1 IRT Refit Expanded (N=178)\",\n    \"description\": \"扩大 v1 IRT 重拟合样本量至 N≥178，最终验证 Path D（large-scale audit）是否可行。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_models\": 178,\n      \"n_items\": 14042,\n      \"3pl_a_pearson_r\": 0.13,\n      \"2pl_a_pearson_r\": -0.03,\n      \"3pl_b_pearson_r\": 0.66,\n      \"a_r_below_threshold\": true,\n      \"conclusion\": \"Path D confirmed dead. Classical MML-EM cannot recover IRT discrimination from LLM response data at available sample sizes.\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: IRT Parameter Recovery (Classical vs PSN-IRT)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"method\",\n          \"N_models\",\n          \"a_pearson_r\",\n          \"b_pearson_r\",\n          \"conclusion\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"MML-EM 3PL (N=63)\",\n            63,\n            0.111,\n            0.626,\n            \"a failure\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MML-EM 3PL (N=178)\",\n            178,\n            0.13,\n            0.66,\n            \"a failure persists\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"PSN-IRT (neural)\",\n            12,\n            \"validated\",\n            \"validated\",\n            \"reference standard\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Path D 的确定性关闭是 paper structure 的关键节点。它确立了 \\\"why ctrl-contam, not leaderboard audit\\\" 的 methodological justification，并为 Future Work 中的 \\\"neural IRT at scale\\\" 提供了动机。\\n\\n\\n即使在 best 档，Path D（leaderboard-scale audit via classical IRT refit）仍然失败。 这不是 experiment failure 而是 honest negative result：classical IRT estimation 需要 hundreds of examinees with similar ability distributions，而 LLM response data 的特殊性（模型间 ability range 极大，item response 非 locally independent） 使得 MML-EM 无法恢复 discrimination parameters。a_r=0.13 << 0.4 threshold 确认 discriminability failure 不是样本量问题而是 structural incompatibility。 这本身是 Claim 3(c) 的贡献：quantifying the estimation challenge for neural IRT。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"4PL vs 3PL Ablation\",\n    \"description\": \"4PL vs 3PL(d=1) 消融实验：量化 d 参数对检测灵敏度的影响。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"mean_power_gain_4pl_vs_3pl\": {\n        \"MMLU\": \"+28pp\",\n        \"HellaSwag\": \"+27pp\",\n        \"GSM8K\": \"+21pp\",\n        \"ARC_C\": \"+15pp\",\n        \"HumanEval\": \"+14pp\"\n      },\n      \"far_4pl\": 0.05,\n      \"far_3pl\": \"0.05-0.17 (inflated)\",\n      \"far_2pl\": \"0.50-1.00 (catastrophic)\",\n      \"items_with_d_lt_095_mmlu\": \"46%\",\n      \"ctrl_contam_4pl_d_15pct\": -3.95,\n      \"ctrl_contam_3pl_d_15pct\": -1.82,\n      \"power_loss_without_d\": \"54%\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: 4PL vs 3PL Detection Performance\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"benchmark\",\n          \"n_items\",\n          \"power_4pl_25pct\",\n          \"power_3pl_25pct\",\n          \"gain\",\n          \"pct_items_d_lt_095\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"MMLU\",\n            14042,\n            0.776,\n            0.329,\n            \"+44.7pp\",\n            \"46%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"HellaSwag\",\n            10042,\n            0.534,\n            0.28,\n            \"+25.4pp\",\n            \"38%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GSM8K\",\n            1319,\n            0.73,\n            0.334,\n            \"+39.6pp\",\n            \"42%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC-C\",\n            295,\n            0.132,\n            0.091,\n            \"+4.1pp\",\n            \"29%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"HumanEval\",\n            164,\n            0.318,\n            0.165,\n            \"+15.3pp\",\n            \"35%\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"4PL ablation 是 methodological rigor 的体现。Reviewer 可能质疑 \\\"为什么不用更简单的 3PL\\\"， 此实验给出定量答案：+28pp average power gain，54% signal loss without d。 结合 exp-4pl-real-data-degradation（r=0.225 between 4PL/3PL lz*）， establishes 4PL 作为 LLM person-fit 的 minimum viable parameterization。\\n\\n\\n4PL 的 d 参数（upper asymptote）对高能力 LLM 至关重要：当 d<1 时，P(correct) 的上限低于 1.0， 高能力模型在这些 items 上 \\\"应该\\\" 答错（按 4PL 预测）。如果忽略 d（设 d=1）， model 预测所有高能力模型都应该答对所有题——这会让 few errors 变成 extreme aberrance（false alarm）。 MMLU 46% items 有 d<0.95 意味着将近一半的题目有上限效应，忽略这些会产生巨大的 FAR 膨胀。 在 best 档下，ctrl-contam 进一步确认：同一污染实验用 3PL 分析时 |d| 从 3.95 降到 1.82， 因为 3PL 的 inflated null variance 稀释了真实信号。这证明 4PL 不是 \\\"nice-to-have\\\" 而是 LLM person-fit 分析的 necessary condition。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Baseline Comparison — Accuracy Z-Score (completed)\",\n    \"description\": \"Accuracy z-score 作为 same-level binary-only baseline 的扩展对比， 整合入完整 baseline comparison 实验中。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"acc_zscore_auroc_5pct\": 0.55,\n      \"acc_zscore_auroc_10pct\": 0.63,\n      \"acc_zscore_auroc_15pct\": 0.71,\n      \"acc_zscore_auroc_25pct\": 0.78,\n      \"lz_star_advantage_over_zscore_5pct\": \"+0.23 AUROC\",\n      \"lz_star_advantage_over_zscore_15pct\": \"+0.21 AUROC\",\n      \"lz_star_advantage_over_zscore_25pct\": \"+0.16 AUROC\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Accuracy z-score 是 \\\"straw-man\\\" 但也是 fair comparison：它是唯一的 same-information-level baseline （binary only, no training data）。lz* 的 consistent +0.16-0.23 AUROC advantage 直接证明 IRT item parameters 提供了有价值的 structural information。\\n\\n\\nAccuracy z-score 只利用 total score（sum of binary responses）而丢失所有 item-level pattern information。lz* 的优势正来自于 item-level aberrance detection： 它区分 \\\"总分高因为答对了该对的题\\\" vs \\\"总分高因为答对了不该对的题\\\"。 在 5% 低污染时，只有 ~700 items（14042×5%）被 contaminate，total score change 微乎其微 （+2-3 pp accuracy），z-score 几乎无法检测。但 lz* 能捕捉到这 700 items 中的 \\\"不可能正确\\\" 模式。 这是 \\\"IRT structure as inductive bias\\\" 的最直接证明。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Domain-Level Analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"MMLU domain-level 分析：按 subject category 分别计算 person-fit，识别污染的 domain 分布。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"gemini_subjects_flagged\": \"50/57 (87.7%)\",\n      \"gemini_contamination_uniform\": true,\n      \"gemini_category_lz_range\": [\n        15.3,\n        21.2\n      ],\n      \"ctrl_contam_domain_uniformity\": \"uniform (as expected, since QLoRA trains on random 15% sample)\",\n      \"ctrl_contam_stem_lz\": 3.8,\n      \"ctrl_contam_humanities_lz\": 3.3,\n      \"ctrl_contam_social_sci_lz\": 3.5,\n      \"ctrl_contam_other_lz\": 3.2,\n      \"doubao_selective_domains\": true,\n      \"doubao_negative_pattern\": \"STEM and Humanities strongly negative, Other positive\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: MMLU Domain-Level lz* (Gemini-1.5 vs Ctrl-Contam)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"domain\",\n          \"gemini_lz\",\n          \"ctrl_contam_15_lz\",\n          \"ctrl_contam_clean_lz\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"STEM\",\n            21.2,\n            3.8,\n            0.1\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Humanities\",\n            17.9,\n            3.3,\n            -0.2\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Social Sciences\",\n            15.9,\n            3.5,\n            0.0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Other\",\n            15.3,\n            3.2,\n            0.1\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Domain analysis 提供了 contamination 的 \\\"spatial resolution\\\"：从 aggregate model-level detection 到 domain-level localization。在 paper 中服务于两个目的：(a) 验证 ctrl-contam 内部一致性 （random sampling → uniform signal），(b) case study 中展示不同 contamination type 的 domain fingerprint。\\n\\n\\nDomain analysis 在 best 档下产生两个 clear findings：(1) Gemini-1.5 的 contamination 是 uniform across domains（所有 subject 都被 memorize），consistent with \\\"bulk training data leak\\\" 而非 \\\"selective domain tuning\\\"；(2) ctrl-contam 模型的 domain-level signal 也是 uniform （因为 QLoRA 训练样本是 randomly sampled across all subjects），验证了实验设计的 internal consistency。 Doubao 的 selective negative pattern 则展示了不同类型的 anomaly：可能是 domain-specific training data 导致某些 domains 泛化过强（lz*<0 = over-consistent pattern）。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Leaderboard Audit (Abandoned)\",\n    \"description\": \"Open LLM Leaderboard v1 大规模 13K+ 模型扫描。因 IRT refit failure 放弃。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"status\": \"ABANDONED\",\n      \"reason\": \"a_r=0.111 discrimination failure makes lz* degenerate to accuracy-like metric at scale\",\n      \"paper_treatment\": \"Data availability noted in Discussion/Future Work; 13K+ per-item data available for future neural IRT estimation\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"ABANDONED。在 paper 中转化为 methodological contribution：量化了 classical vs neural IRT 在 LLM context 中的 gap，为 future work 提供了 concrete roadmap（13K+ data available, awaiting better estimation methods）。\\n\\n即使在 best 档，leaderboard audit 仍然 abandoned。这不影响 best 档的叙事， 因为 ctrl-contam 提供了比 leaderboard audit 更强的 ground-truth validation。 Audit 的 abandonment 本身是 honest negative result (Claim 3c)：classical IRT 的 sample size requirement 与 LLM evaluation ecosystem 不兼容。 Paper 中将其定位为 \\\"future work when neural IRT estimation at scale becomes feasible\\\"。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":1066,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1066}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JxWdFwFH6hRNN4Rw4nXYFj","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — irt_personfit_contam\n2\t\n3\t## Target Venue\n4\t- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (用户确认；ARR submission DDL 5/25 — 需确认可行性)\n5\t- Fallback: AAAI 2027 (abstract 7/21, full paper 7/28, ~10 weeks)\n6\t- Backup: ICLR 2027 (~Sep 2026, ~17 weeks)\n7\t\n8\t## Core Claims (3 条)\n9\t\n10\t**Claim 1 (Minimal-Information Detection Framework + Controlled Validation)**:\n11\tIRT person-fit statistics provide a principled contamination detection framework at the minimal-information operating point — requiring only binary response patterns. Simulation establishes high theoretical detection power (97.9% on MMLU-scale benchmarks), and bootstrap null distributions are well-calibrated (near-perfect N(0,1) for large benchmarks, KS reject rate 8.3%). In simulation, lz* matches or outperforms supervised binary classifiers (LR/RF with oracle labels) at low contamination (5-10%), leveraging IRT structure as inductive bias. Controlled contamination experiments (QLoRA SFT injection on Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct) validate the framework on real models: at 15% contamination, |Cohen's d|=3.85 with clear seen/unseen memorization fingerprint (seen lz*≈0 vs unseen=3.1). θ-fixed analysis reveals a θ-shift boundary condition: when θ is re-estimated on contaminated data, detection sensitivity degrades at high contamination (50%), but fixing θ to pre-contamination baseline restores monotonic dose-response (ratio=2.93). The memorization fraction (~38% at 15% contamination) quantifies the SFT generalization effect — the gap between theoretical power and actual detection signal.\n12\t\n13\t**Claim 2 (Detection Characterization)**:\n14\tDetection power is a predictable function of benchmark size (n_items) and contamination level, with two distinct signal regimes: partial contamination produces aberrant patterns (lz* << 0), full contamination produces over-consistent patterns (lz* >> 0). For sufficiently large benchmarks (≥10K items), theoretical power exceeds 90% at 15% contamination. Note: power function gives an **upper bound** (assumes all contaminated items produce aberrant signal); SFT generalization reduces effective signal — ctrl-contam measures actual memorization fraction to derive adjusted (\"expected\") power. Both upper bound and adjusted power should be reported.\n15\t\n16\t**Claim 3 (Empirical Findings from Real LLM Data)**:\n17\tThree empirical findings from applying IRT person-fit to real LLM response data: (a) **Universal 4PL model misfit** — nearly all (model, benchmark) cells produce extreme lz* values (|lz*| >> 5, 57/60 cells flagged after BH-FDR correction), revealing that LLM response patterns fundamentally differ from classical test-taker patterns. This is a genuine property of LLM responses (bootstrap null is well-calibrated), not a statistical artifact. The simulation-to-reality gap motivates the Δlz* design. (b) **PSN-IRT 12-model case study** — detailed anomaly profiles with validated 4PL parameters (Gemini-1.5: 100% MMLU accuracy, lz*=+34.75, θ=0.78; selective vs uniform misfit patterns across benchmarks; Ward clustering reveals contamination typology). (c) **IRT parameter estimation challenges** — MML-EM refit from v1 leaderboard data (N=63→178, covering all available models) yields b_r=0.66 (partial difficulty validation) but a_r≈0.13 (discrimination failure, well below 0.2 threshold), quantifying the sample size gap between classical IRT and neural IRT estimation in LLM contexts. 13K+ model per-item data is publicly available for future large-scale audits once estimation challenges are resolved.\n18\t\n19\t## Story Spine\n20\t\n21\t**Problem**: Benchmark contamination undermines LLM evaluation reliability. As benchmarks proliferate and training corpora grow, contamination risk increases, but all existing detection methods require privileged access — training data (n-gram overlap), token probabilities (Min-K%, MIA), model weights (internal probing), or specially crafted prompts (Time Travel). A contaminated LLM is functionally analogous to an examinee with item preknowledge, yet no work has connected the mature psychometric literature on cheating detection to LLM benchmark integrity.\n22\t\n23\t**Existing approaches & gaps**: Detection methods circa 2026 span five families: time-based partition, MIA/Min-K%++ (ICLR 2024), Time Travel probing (ICLR 2024 Spotlight), ConStat performance-based testing (NeurIPS 2024), and CoDeC in-context learning effects (ICLR 2026). Wang et al. (2025) show all MIA-based methods fail under post-RL contamination. Critically, ALL require more than binary response patterns — no method operates at the minimal-information level.\n24\t\n25\t**Our framing**: We establish the minimal-information operating point on the contamination detection frontier. By repurposing IRT person-fit statistics — developed over decades for detecting exam cheating — we ask: \"What can be detected from binary response patterns alone?\" We show: (1) in simulation, person-fit statistics achieve high detection power (97.9% on MMLU-scale benchmarks) with well-calibrated null distributions; (2) in real LLM data, response patterns universally deviate from 4PL predictions — the statistical framework is sound, but LLMs genuinely violate IRT assumptions (local independence, unidimensionality), producing extreme lz* values across nearly all models; (3) controlled contamination experiments leverage this by measuring Δlz* between clean and contaminated models — since the null is well-calibrated, within-model shifts are statistically interpretable. The universal model misfit finding is itself a contribution — it reveals that LLM response patterns are fundamentally different from classical test-taker patterns.\n26\t\n27\t**Headline result template**: \"Using only binary response patterns, IRT-FIT achieves 97.9% simulated detection power on MMLU (14K items) with well-calibrated null distributions. In simulation, lz* matches or outperforms supervised binary classifiers (LR/RF with oracle labels) at practically relevant low contamination levels (5-10%), leveraging IRT structure as an inductive bias that compensates for the absence of labeled data. While all LLMs exhibit universal 4PL model misfit (a finding in itself), controlled experiments show contamination induces a measurable Δlz* shift of X SD above each model's baseline misfit, enabling detection even in the presence of universal misfit.\"\n28\t\n29\t## Venue Fit Risks\n30\t\n31\t- **EMNLP**: NLP evaluation methodology fits well. Risk: \"no new NLP model/technique\" → mitigate by positioning as foundational evaluation methodology with direct community impact (leaderboard integrity).\n32\t- **AAAI**: PSN-IRT was AAAI 2026 Oral — strong psychometrics+AI audience. Risk: less NLP-specific reviewer pool.\n33\t- **Cross-discipline concern**: IRT/psychometrics may be unfamiliar to ML reviewers → need self-contained exposition in Section 3 (IRT background), avoid jargon, provide intuitive explanations.\n34\t\n35\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns & Planned Responses\n36\t\n37\t| # | Concern | Response Strategy | Supporting Experiment |\n38\t|---|---------|------------------|----------------------|\n39\t| R1 | \"Just applying existing IRT to LLMs\" | Frame as establishing new operating point, not cross-domain transfer. Person-fit for contamination is unexplored. Downgrade \"cross-domain\" from contribution to background. | — |\n40\t| R2 | \"No ground truth contamination labels\" | Controlled contamination experiment (fine-tune clean models on benchmark items). Phase B anomalies are converging evidence, not proof. | exp-ctrl-contam |\n41\t| R3 | \"Power too low for small benchmarks\" | Present power function analysis as contribution, not limitation. Derive theoretical relationship. | exp-power-theory |\n42\t| R4 | \"Only 12 models\" | 12 models with validated 4PL parameters provide detailed anomaly profiles. Universal misfit (57/60 flagged) spans sufficient models to establish the pattern. 13K+ v1 per-item data availability discussed as future work. Ctrl-contam covers 4-5 model families. | exp-ctrl-contam, phase_b_personfit |\n43\t| R5 | \"SFT generalization smooths signal\" | Controlled experiment includes domain-level analysis. Discuss hard-item contamination resistance. | exp-ctrl-contam |\n44\t| R6 | \"Absolute lz* thresholds don't work on real data\" | Bootstrap null is well-calibrated (KS pass for large benchmarks); the issue is LLMs genuinely deviate from 4PL. Universal model misfit is a finding, not an artifact. Δlz* leverages the well-calibrated null for within-model comparisons. | exp-ctrl-contam, exp-empirical-null |\n45\t| R7 | \"Post-RL contamination?\" | Hypothesis test: GRPO after SFT contamination on Qwen 3.5-9B. | exp-post-rl |\n46\t| R8 | \"4PL vs 3PL — does d parameter matter?\" | Ablation comparing 4PL vs 3PL(d=1) detection sensitivity. | exp-4pl-ablation |\n47\t| R9 | \"No same-level binary-only baselines\" | accuracy z-score (done, lz* dominates 57/60 vs 4/60) + ML classifier on binary vectors (simulation train, ctrl-contam test). lz* advantage: per-cell statistic needing no training data. | exp-accuracy-zscore-baseline, exp-ml-classifier-baseline |\n48\t| R10 | \"Leaderboard audit baseline unreliable\" | Leaderboard audit abandoned (D011). ctrl-contam is the validated detection. 12-model case study uses PSN-IRT validated parameters directly (no baseline estimation needed). v1 data availability noted as future work. | exp-ctrl-contam |\n49\t| R11 | \"Power function is upper bound\" | Report both theoretical upper bound AND adjusted power (memorization fraction from ctrl-contam seen/unseen split). Gap = SFT generalization effect quantification. | exp-ctrl-contam, exp-power-theory |\n50\t\n51\t## Key Narrative Elements (from External Review + Distillation)\n52\t\n53\t1. **Detection frontier framing** — Systematically rank all methods by information access level (binary < rephrased retest < token probs < logits < weights). IRT-FIT defines the bottom of this frontier.\n54\t2. **Definitional pivot (à la ConStat)** — \"All prior contamination detection methods require privileged access. We ask a more fundamental question: what can be detected from binary response patterns alone?\" This reframes our work as problem reformulation, not just cross-domain transfer.\n55\t3. **RL-robustness as structural advantage** — Wang et al. (ICLR 2026) proves all 10 log-prob methods ≈ random on RL-trained reasoning models. Person-fit operates on binary response patterns, not token distributions — structurally immune to RL-induced distributional shifts. This is our strongest motivation against log-prob baselines.\n56\t4. **Scalability potential (deferred to future work)** — 13K+ v1 per-item data publicly available. IRT-FIT is uniquely suited for retrospective audit (only needs archival binary data). BUT: current paper does NOT include large-scale audit (D011: IRT refit failed). Mention data availability + roadmap in Discussion/Future Work. NEVER claim \"leaderboard audit\" or \"large-scale detection\" in current paper.\n57\t5. **Inverted-U as theoretical characterization** — Not just empirical observation. Derive from: (a) contamination→0%: signal drowned in sampling noise; (b) contamination→100%: identifiability collapse. Theory gives R²=0.957 fit.\n58\t6. **Scope precision** — Target: \"intentional SFT contamination / leaderboard gaming\". Pretraining exposure → smooth distributional improvement, not in scope. Honest scoping > vague claims.\n59\t7. **Terminology guard** — NEVER use \"binary information bottleneck\" or \"information-theoretic lower bound for all binary-only methods.\" We can only claim lz* (a specific statistic) has limitations under SFT generalization — NOT that all binary-only methods fail. Correct framing: \"IRT person-fit as a principled framework at the minimal-information operating point.\"\n60\t8. **Validation hierarchy** — ctrl-contam = primary validation (ground truth, same model clean vs contaminated); 12-model case study = empirical findings (no ground truth, but validated parameters); v1 data = future work roadmap. Paper structure should reflect this priority.\n61\t9. **lz* measures memorization, not generalization** — lz* detects aberrant patterns (memorization signature), not smooth ability improvement (generalization). This is a feature: it distinguishes genuine learning from rote memorization. Power function gives upper bound; ctrl-contam measures actual memorization fraction.\n62\t10. **Negative results as contributions** — D007 (universal misfit) and D008 (empirical null well-calibrated) are \"honest negative results that become positive contributions\": universal misfit is a novel finding about LLM response patterns; the simulation-reality gap motivates Δlz* and quantifies SFT generalization. D011 (MML-EM refit failure) is a methodological caveat (classical vs neural IRT sample requirements). D009 (item alignment) is a data engineering detail (1 sentence in Data section). Present negatives with the framing: \"the gap between where IRT works perfectly (simulation) and where it struggles (real LLM data) is itself informative.\"\n63\t11. **ctrl-contam actual results (D015)** — contam_15 |d|=3.85 (strong), contam_50 non-monotonic under free-θ but **monotonic under θ-fixed** (ratio=2.93). θ-shift is the mechanism: contamination→higher θ_MLE→absorbs aberrance signal. Frame as \"principled detection with quantified operating characteristics + θ-shift boundary condition.\" Headline: \"We don't just detect — we characterize, including the conditions under which detection degrades.\" Do NOT claim \"state-of-the-art detection.\"\n64\t12. **θ-shift as methodological contribution (D015)** — Person-fit sensitivity degrades when θ is re-estimated on contaminated data. This is a novel finding for contamination detection: (a) θ-fixed analysis recovers monotonic dose-response, (b) the θ-shift magnitude (0.47 at 50% contamination) quantifies the confound, (c) practical implication: use pre-contamination θ baseline or cross-validated θ. Present as a contribution, not a limitation.\n65\t13. **seen/unseen split as strongest signal** — contam_15 seen lz*≈0 (memorized items look \"normal\") vs unseen lz*=3.1. This is the clearest contamination fingerprint: items that should produce aberrant responses instead produce expected responses. More interpretable than aggregate Δlz*.\n66\t\n67\t## Writing Strategy (from Distillation)\n68\t\n69\t- **Story type**: \"跨界迁移型\" — unused in 0/8 peer papers. Our unique angle.\n70\t- **Figure 1**: Problem illustration (dual-panel: contaminated vs clean response pattern). Use psychometric hook — impossible response pattern (hard items right, easy wrong).\n71\t- **Contribution structure**: 3 contributions (method + characterization + empirical findings), escalating scope. Standard in 5/8 papers.\n72\t- **Result tables**: Row=methods, col=datasets×metrics. Bold-best. Average column.\n73\t- **Numbered findings**: Adopt PSN-IRT's \"Key Discoveries\" strategy for scannable presentation.\n74\t- **CIs as differentiator**: 6/8 peer papers report no variance. Our bootstrap CIs are a competitive advantage.\n75\t- **Baseline count**: Peer median ~5. Target ≥5 baselines.\n76\t\n77\t## Evidence Summary\n78\t\n79\t- **Phase A (simulation)**: Null check passed (4PL compatible with lz* theory). MMLU power@15%=97.9%. Power ∝ n_items confirmed. Simulation results stand — they establish theoretical detection capacity within the 4PL model.\n80\t- **Phase B (real data)**: Gemini-1.5 MMLU acc=1.000, θ=0.78, lz*=+34.75. Cross-benchmark anomaly profiles identified.\n81\t- **Empirical null analysis (exp-empirical-null)**: Bootstrap null distributions are well-calibrated — MMLU null mean bias 0.041, std 1.003, KS reject 8.3%. The statistical framework is sound. 57/60 real-data cells flagged because LLM lz* values are genuinely extreme (|lz*| >> 5), not because of null miscalibration. Universal 4PL model misfit is a real property of LLM response patterns.\n82\t- **Calibration gap reframed (D007→D008)**: The gap is not \"null is biased\" but \"real LLM data genuinely deviates from 4PL\". This strengthens Δlz* approach: well-calibrated null means within-model shifts are statistically meaningful.\n83\t- **Controlled contamination (exp-ctrl-contam-pilot, D015)**: Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct × MMLU, 4 conditions (0%×2 seeds, 15%, 50%). Key results: (a) contam_15 |Cohen's d|=3.85 (strong detection signal); (b) free-θ dose-response non-monotonic (contam_50 Δlz*=1.53 < contam_15 Δlz*=3.97) due to θ-shift confound; (c) **θ-fixed analysis restores monotonicity** (Δlz*_fixed: contam_15=+2.96, contam_50=+8.67, ratio=2.93); (d) seen/unseen split: contam_15 seen lz*≈0 vs unseen=3.1 (clear memorization fingerprint); (e) memorization_fraction=0.38 (15%) and 0.29 (50%). θ-shift mechanism: contamination raises θ_MLE, absorbing aberrance signal — this is a methodological contribution.\n84\t- **4PL real-data degradation**: 3PL(d=1) vs 4PL lz* correlation r=0.225, RMSE=68.41. d parameter essential for high-ability models (DeepSeek-V3 Δ=357). Complements simulation ablation (+14-27pp power gain).\n85\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f4e042fb-0a90-4bbe-8eb1-3013bf130d8d","uuid":"95347878-5e7d-473d-8584-3f6a5be88b0f","timestamp":"2026-05-20T19:22:28.205Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0519-3/projects/irt_personfit_contam/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260520T190245/best/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — irt_personfit_contam\n\n## Target Venue\n- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (用户确认；ARR submission DDL 5/25 — 需确认可行性)\n- Fallback: AAAI 2027 (abstract 7/21, full paper 7/28, ~10 weeks)\n- Backup: ICLR 2027 (~Sep 2026, ~17 weeks)\n\n## Core Claims (3 条)\n\n**Claim 1 (Minimal-Information Detection Framework + Controlled Validation)**:\nIRT person-fit statistics provide a principled contamination detection framework at the minimal-information operating point — requiring only binary response patterns. Simulation establishes high theoretical detection power (97.9% on MMLU-scale benchmarks), and bootstrap null distributions are well-calibrated (near-perfect N(0,1) for large benchmarks, KS reject rate 8.3%). In simulation, lz* matches or outperforms supervised binary classifiers (LR/RF with oracle labels) at low contamination (5-10%), leveraging IRT structure as inductive bias. Controlled contamination experiments (QLoRA SFT injection on Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct) validate the framework on real models: at 15% contamination, |Cohen's d|=3.85 with clear seen/unseen memorization fingerprint (seen lz*≈0 vs unseen=3.1). θ-fixed analysis reveals a θ-shift boundary condition: when θ is re-estimated on contaminated data, detection sensitivity degrades at high contamination (50%), but fixing θ to pre-contamination baseline restores monotonic dose-response (ratio=2.93). The memorization fraction (~38% at 15% contamination) quantifies the SFT generalization effect — the gap between theoretical power and actual detection signal.\n\n**Claim 2 (Detection Characterization)**:\nDetection power is a predictable function of benchmark size (n_items) and contamination level, with two distinct signal regimes: partial contamination produces aberrant patterns (lz* << 0), full contamination produces over-consistent patterns (lz* >> 0). For sufficiently large benchmarks (≥10K items), theoretical power exceeds 90% at 15% contamination. Note: power function gives an **upper bound** (assumes all contaminated items produce aberrant signal); SFT generalization reduces effective signal — ctrl-contam measures actual memorization fraction to derive adjusted (\"expected\") power. Both upper bound and adjusted power should be reported.\n\n**Claim 3 (Empirical Findings from Real LLM Data)**:\nThree empirical findings from applying IRT person-fit to real LLM response data: (a) **Universal 4PL model misfit** — nearly all (model, benchmark) cells produce extreme lz* values (|lz*| >> 5, 57/60 cells flagged after BH-FDR correction), revealing that LLM response patterns fundamentally differ from classical test-taker patterns. This is a genuine property of LLM responses (bootstrap null is well-calibrated), not a statistical artifact. The simulation-to-reality gap motivates the Δlz* design. (b) **PSN-IRT 12-model case study** — detailed anomaly profiles with validated 4PL parameters (Gemini-1.5: 100% MMLU accuracy, lz*=+34.75, θ=0.78; selective vs uniform misfit patterns across benchmarks; Ward clustering reveals contamination typology). (c) **IRT parameter estimation challenges** — MML-EM refit from v1 leaderboard data (N=63→178, covering all available models) yields b_r=0.66 (partial difficulty validation) but a_r≈0.13 (discrimination failure, well below 0.2 threshold), quantifying the sample size gap between classical IRT and neural IRT estimation in LLM contexts. 13K+ model per-item data is publicly available for future large-scale audits once estimation challenges are resolved.\n\n## Story Spine\n\n**Problem**: Benchmark contamination undermines LLM evaluation reliability. As benchmarks proliferate and training corpora grow, contamination risk increases, but all existing detection methods require privileged access — training data (n-gram overlap), token probabilities (Min-K%, MIA), model weights (internal probing), or specially crafted prompts (Time Travel). A contaminated LLM is functionally analogous to an examinee with item preknowledge, yet no work has connected the mature psychometric literature on cheating detection to LLM benchmark integrity.\n\n**Existing approaches & gaps**: Detection methods circa 2026 span five families: time-based partition, MIA/Min-K%++ (ICLR 2024), Time Travel probing (ICLR 2024 Spotlight), ConStat performance-based testing (NeurIPS 2024), and CoDeC in-context learning effects (ICLR 2026). Wang et al. (2025) show all MIA-based methods fail under post-RL contamination. Critically, ALL require more than binary response patterns — no method operates at the minimal-information level.\n\n**Our framing**: We establish the minimal-information operating point on the contamination detection frontier. By repurposing IRT person-fit statistics — developed over decades for detecting exam cheating — we ask: \"What can be detected from binary response patterns alone?\" We show: (1) in simulation, person-fit statistics achieve high detection power (97.9% on MMLU-scale benchmarks) with well-calibrated null distributions; (2) in real LLM data, response patterns universally deviate from 4PL predictions — the statistical framework is sound, but LLMs genuinely violate IRT assumptions (local independence, unidimensionality), producing extreme lz* values across nearly all models; (3) controlled contamination experiments leverage this by measuring Δlz* between clean and contaminated models — since the null is well-calibrated, within-model shifts are statistically interpretable. The universal model misfit finding is itself a contribution — it reveals that LLM response patterns are fundamentally different from classical test-taker patterns.\n\n**Headline result template**: \"Using only binary response patterns, IRT-FIT achieves 97.9% simulated detection power on MMLU (14K items) with well-calibrated null distributions. In simulation, lz* matches or outperforms supervised binary classifiers (LR/RF with oracle labels) at practically relevant low contamination levels (5-10%), leveraging IRT structure as an inductive bias that compensates for the absence of labeled data. While all LLMs exhibit universal 4PL model misfit (a finding in itself), controlled experiments show contamination induces a measurable Δlz* shift of X SD above each model's baseline misfit, enabling detection even in the presence of universal misfit.\"\n\n## Venue Fit Risks\n\n- **EMNLP**: NLP evaluation methodology fits well. Risk: \"no new NLP model/technique\" → mitigate by positioning as foundational evaluation methodology with direct community impact (leaderboard integrity).\n- **AAAI**: PSN-IRT was AAAI 2026 Oral — strong psychometrics+AI audience. Risk: less NLP-specific reviewer pool.\n- **Cross-discipline concern**: IRT/psychometrics may be unfamiliar to ML reviewers → need self-contained exposition in Section 3 (IRT background), avoid jargon, provide intuitive explanations.\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns & Planned Responses\n\n| # | Concern | Response Strategy | Supporting Experiment |\n|---|---------|------------------|----------------------|\n| R1 | \"Just applying existing IRT to LLMs\" | Frame as establishing new operating point, not cross-domain transfer. Person-fit for contamination is unexplored. Downgrade \"cross-domain\" from contribution to background. | — |\n| R2 | \"No ground truth contamination labels\" | Controlled contamination experiment (fine-tune clean models on benchmark items). Phase B anomalies are converging evidence, not proof. | exp-ctrl-contam |\n| R3 | \"Power too low for small benchmarks\" | Present power function analysis as contribution, not limitation. Derive theoretical relationship. | exp-power-theory |\n| R4 | \"Only 12 models\" | 12 models with validated 4PL parameters provide detailed anomaly profiles. Universal misfit (57/60 flagged) spans sufficient models to establish the pattern. 13K+ v1 per-item data availability discussed as future work. Ctrl-contam covers 4-5 model families. | exp-ctrl-contam, phase_b_personfit |\n| R5 | \"SFT generalization smooths signal\" | Controlled experiment includes domain-level analysis. Discuss hard-item contamination resistance. | exp-ctrl-contam |\n| R6 | \"Absolute lz* thresholds don't work on real data\" | Bootstrap null is well-calibrated (KS pass for large benchmarks); the issue is LLMs genuinely deviate from 4PL. Universal model misfit is a finding, not an artifact. Δlz* leverages the well-calibrated null for within-model comparisons. | exp-ctrl-contam, exp-empirical-null |\n| R7 | \"Post-RL contamination?\" | Hypothesis test: GRPO after SFT contamination on Qwen 3.5-9B. | exp-post-rl |\n| R8 | \"4PL vs 3PL — does d parameter matter?\" | Ablation comparing 4PL vs 3PL(d=1) detection sensitivity. | exp-4pl-ablation |\n| R9 | \"No same-level binary-only baselines\" | accuracy z-score (done, lz* dominates 57/60 vs 4/60) + ML classifier on binary vectors (simulation train, ctrl-contam test). lz* advantage: per-cell statistic needing no training data. | exp-accuracy-zscore-baseline, exp-ml-classifier-baseline |\n| R10 | \"Leaderboard audit baseline unreliable\" | Leaderboard audit abandoned (D011). ctrl-contam is the validated detection. 12-model case study uses PSN-IRT validated parameters directly (no baseline estimation needed). v1 data availability noted as future work. | exp-ctrl-contam |\n| R11 | \"Power function is upper bound\" | Report both theoretical upper bound AND adjusted power (memorization fraction from ctrl-contam seen/unseen split). Gap = SFT generalization effect quantification. | exp-ctrl-contam, exp-power-theory |\n\n## Key Narrative Elements (from External Review + Distillation)\n\n1. **Detection frontier framing** — Systematically rank all methods by information access level (binary < rephrased retest < token probs < logits < weights). IRT-FIT defines the bottom of this frontier.\n2. **Definitional pivot (à la ConStat)** — \"All prior contamination detection methods require privileged access. We ask a more fundamental question: what can be detected from binary response patterns alone?\" This reframes our work as problem reformulation, not just cross-domain transfer.\n3. **RL-robustness as structural advantage** — Wang et al. (ICLR 2026) proves all 10 log-prob methods ≈ random on RL-trained reasoning models. Person-fit operates on binary response patterns, not token distributions — structurally immune to RL-induced distributional shifts. This is our strongest motivation against log-prob baselines.\n4. **Scalability potential (deferred to future work)** — 13K+ v1 per-item data publicly available. IRT-FIT is uniquely suited for retrospective audit (only needs archival binary data). BUT: current paper does NOT include large-scale audit (D011: IRT refit failed). Mention data availability + roadmap in Discussion/Future Work. NEVER claim \"leaderboard audit\" or \"large-scale detection\" in current paper.\n5. **Inverted-U as theoretical characterization** — Not just empirical observation. Derive from: (a) contamination→0%: signal drowned in sampling noise; (b) contamination→100%: identifiability collapse. Theory gives R²=0.957 fit.\n6. **Scope precision** — Target: \"intentional SFT contamination / leaderboard gaming\". Pretraining exposure → smooth distributional improvement, not in scope. Honest scoping > vague claims.\n7. **Terminology guard** — NEVER use \"binary information bottleneck\" or \"information-theoretic lower bound for all binary-only methods.\" We can only claim lz* (a specific statistic) has limitations under SFT generalization — NOT that all binary-only methods fail. Correct framing: \"IRT person-fit as a principled framework at the minimal-information operating point.\"\n8. **Validation hierarchy** — ctrl-contam = primary validation (ground truth, same model clean vs contaminated); 12-model case study = empirical findings (no ground truth, but validated parameters); v1 data = future work roadmap. Paper structure should reflect this priority.\n9. **lz* measures memorization, not generalization** — lz* detects aberrant patterns (memorization signature), not smooth ability improvement (generalization). This is a feature: it distinguishes genuine learning from rote memorization. Power function gives upper bound; ctrl-contam measures actual memorization fraction.\n10. **Negative results as contributions** — D007 (universal misfit) and D008 (empirical null well-calibrated) are \"honest negative results that become positive contributions\": universal misfit is a novel finding about LLM response patterns; the simulation-reality gap motivates Δlz* and quantifies SFT generalization. D011 (MML-EM refit failure) is a methodological caveat (classical vs neural IRT sample requirements). D009 (item alignment) is a data engineering detail (1 sentence in Data section). Present negatives with the framing: \"the gap between where IRT works perfectly (simulation) and where it struggles (real LLM data) is itself informative.\"\n11. **ctrl-contam actual results (D015)** — contam_15 |d|=3.85 (strong), contam_50 non-monotonic under free-θ but **monotonic under θ-fixed** (ratio=2.93). θ-shift is the mechanism: contamination→higher θ_MLE→absorbs aberrance signal. Frame as \"principled detection with quantified operating characteristics + θ-shift boundary condition.\" Headline: \"We don't just detect — we characterize, including the conditions under which detection degrades.\" Do NOT claim \"state-of-the-art detection.\"\n12. **θ-shift as methodological contribution (D015)** — Person-fit sensitivity degrades when θ is re-estimated on contaminated data. This is a novel finding for contamination detection: (a) θ-fixed analysis recovers monotonic dose-response, (b) the θ-shift magnitude (0.47 at 50% contamination) quantifies the confound, (c) practical implication: use pre-contamination θ baseline or cross-validated θ. Present as a contribution, not a limitation.\n13. **seen/unseen split as strongest signal** — contam_15 seen lz*≈0 (memorized items look \"normal\") vs unseen lz*=3.1. This is the clearest contamination fingerprint: items that should produce aberrant responses instead produce expected responses. More interpretable than aggregate Δlz*.\n\n## Writing Strategy (from Distillation)\n\n- **Story type**: \"跨界迁移型\" — unused in 0/8 peer papers. Our unique angle.\n- **Figure 1**: Problem illustration (dual-panel: contaminated vs clean response pattern). Use psychometric hook — impossible response pattern (hard items right, easy wrong).\n- **Contribution structure**: 3 contributions (method + characterization + empirical findings), escalating scope. Standard in 5/8 papers.\n- **Result tables**: Row=methods, col=datasets×metrics. Bold-best. Average column.\n- **Numbered findings**: Adopt PSN-IRT's \"Key Discoveries\" strategy for scannable presentation.\n- **CIs as differentiator**: 6/8 peer papers report no variance. Our bootstrap CIs are a competitive advantage.\n- **Baseline count**: Peer median ~5. Target ≥5 baselines.\n\n## Evidence Summary\n\n- **Phase A (simulation)**: Null check passed (4PL compatible with lz* theory). MMLU power@15%=97.9%. Power ∝ n_items confirmed. Simulation results stand — they establish theoretical detection capacity within the 4PL model.\n- **Phase B (real data)**: Gemini-1.5 MMLU acc=1.000, θ=0.78, lz*=+34.75. Cross-benchmark anomaly profiles identified.\n- **Empirical null analysis (exp-empirical-null)**: Bootstrap null distributions are well-calibrated — MMLU null mean bias 0.041, std 1.003, KS reject 8.3%. The statistical framework is sound. 57/60 real-data cells flagged because LLM lz* values are genuinely extreme (|lz*| >> 5), not because of null miscalibration. Universal 4PL model misfit is a real property of LLM response patterns.\n- **Calibration gap reframed (D007→D008)**: The gap is not \"null is biased\" but \"real LLM data genuinely deviates from 4PL\". This strengthens Δlz* approach: well-calibrated null means within-model shifts are statistically meaningful.\n- **Controlled contamination (exp-ctrl-contam-pilot, D015)**: Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct × MMLU, 4 conditions (0%×2 seeds, 15%, 50%). Key results: (a) contam_15 |Cohen's d|=3.85 (strong detection signal); (b) free-θ dose-response non-monotonic (contam_50 Δlz*=1.53 < contam_15 Δlz*=3.97) due to θ-shift confound; (c) **θ-fixed analysis restores monotonicity** (Δlz*_fixed: contam_15=+2.96, contam_50=+8.67, ratio=2.93); (d) seen/unseen split: contam_15 seen lz*≈0 vs unseen=3.1 (clear memorization fingerprint); (e) memorization_fraction=0.38 (15%) and 0.29 (50%). θ-shift mechanism: contamination raises θ_MLE, absorbing aberrance signal — this is a methodological contribution.\n- **4PL real-data degradation**: 3PL(d=1) vs 4PL lz* correlation r=0.225, RMSE=68.41. d parameter essential for high-ability models (DeepSeek-V3 Δ=357). Complements simulation ablation (+14-27pp power gain).\n","numLines":85,"startLine":1,"totalLines":85}}}
